hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7201","And Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, from Abu Hilal, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr and Umar, and my stronger supposition is the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), cut for a shield worth five dirhams."
"7202","Rawh ibn Hatim and Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Adami narrated to us, Dawud ibn Shabib narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever intends the humiliation of Quraysh, Allah will humiliate him. And this hadith and the hadith of the shield are only known through Abu Hilal, from Qatada, from Anas, except that the hadith of the shield was narrated by Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr, from Shuba, from Qatada, from Anas."
"7203","Abu Kamil narrated to us, al-Qannad narrated to us, whose name is Ibrahim ibn Sulayman Abu Ismail, Qatada narrated to us, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution with a mudd and bathe with a sa."
"7204","And with it: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a dead sheep and said: The world is more insignificant to Allah than this is to its owners. And these two hadiths, we do not know anyone who narrated them from Qatada, from Anas, except Abu Ismail, and there was no harm in him; Affan and others narrated from him. And these two hadiths, we do not know anyone who narrated them from him other than Abu Kamil. The hadith: He performs ablution with a mudd and bathes with a sa, is an error; Qatada narrated it from Safiyya, from Aisha, and Qatada narrated it from Muadha, from Aisha."
"7205","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, al-Khalil ibn Umar narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wealth is not from abundance of goods. It was said: Then what is wealth? He said: Wealth of the soul. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatada, from Anas, except Umar ibn Ibrahim."
"7206","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Shaddad ibn Fayyad narrated to us, Umar ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The Black Stone is of the stones of Paradise. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatada, from Anas, except Umar ibn Ibrahim, and he is not a memorizer; only what is not preserved from others is written from his hadith."
"7207","Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Bara ibn Yazid al-Ghanawi narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is near that Allah will fill your hands from the non-Arabs, then make them lions who do not flee, fighting your fighters and eating your fay. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except from this route, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Qatada, from Anas, except al-Bara ibn Yazid al-Ghanawi, and there is no harm in him; a large group of scholars narrated from him and accepted his hadith."
"7208","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Anas: that the sandals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had two straps. And this hadith is only preserved from the hadith of Hammam, though it reached me that Ibn al-Mubarak narrated it from Hisham, from Qatada, from Anas."
"7209","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is more joyful at the repentance of His servant than one of you finding his camel in a desert land after losing it. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Qatada, from Anas, except from the hadith of Hammam."
"7210","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to strike his shoulders. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Hammam, from Qatada, from Anas."
"7211","And with it: that Umm Sulaym sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a basket with ripe dates upon it, and he kept taking a handful and sending it to one of his wives, then taking a handful and sending it to one of his wives, then sat and ate the eating of a man known to desire it. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Hammam, from Qatada, from Anas."
"7212","And with it: that a man entered the prayer and said: Praise be to Allah, much, good, blessed praise therein. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer, he said: Which of you is the speaker of such and such words? The people fell silent, so he said it three times. Then a man of the people said: I said it, and I intended by it only good. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Twelve angels hastened to it, racing as to how to write it, until they asked their Lord, and He said: Write it as My servant said. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Anas except from the hadith of Qatada, and Hammam and Hammad ibn Salama narrated it from Qatada."
"7213","And with it, he said: I asked Anas: How many Hajj did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform? He said: One Hajj, and he performed four Umras: his Umra from al-Hudaybiya, his Umra in Dhu al-Qada, his Umra from al-Jirana when he divided the spoils of Hunayn, and his Umra with his Hajj. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Qatada, from Anas, except from the hadith of Hammam."
"7214","And with it, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a camel-driver with a beautiful voice, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Gently, O Anjasha, do not break the glass vessels, meaning the weak women. And this hadith is narrated from Anas through routes, while we do not know it narrated from Qatada except from the hadith of Hammam."
"7215","And with it: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from madness, leprosy, vitiligo and evil diseases."
"7216","Raja ibn Muhammad al-Saqati narrated to us, Said ibn Amir narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prescribed for what the sky and springs water a tenth, and what is watered by camels half a tenth. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Anas except from this route; the memorizers narrated it from Qatada, from Abu al-Khalil, while Said ibn Amir said: From Hammam, from Qatada, from Anas."
"7217","Muhammad ibn Thalaba narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sawa narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The sleeve of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached to the wrist. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Anas except Qatada, nor from Qatada except Hammam, nor from Hammam except Ibn al-Sawa, nor from Ibn Sawa except Muhammad ibn Thalaba."
"7218","Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whom do you count as childless among you? They said: One who has no child. He said: Rather he is one who has no predecessor. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Qatada, from Anas, except from the hadith of Hammam, nor do we know it narrated from Hammam except from the hadith of Yaqub ibn Ishaq."
"7219","Al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Abd Rabbih ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves extension in his term and increase in his provision, let him fear Allah and join his kinship. And this hadith was narrated from Anas through other than one route, while we do not know it narrated from Qatada, from Anas, except from the hadith of Hammam."
"7220","Al-Abbas ibn Jafar narrated to us, Fahd ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of the believer is like the ear of grain, inclining at times and standing at times."
"7221","And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Fahd ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of the believer is like the ear of grain turned by the wind. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Hammam except Fahd ibn Hayyan."
"7222","Some of our companions narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in what he relates from his Lord, the Blessed and Exalted: Whoever I take his two precious ones and he is patient and seeks reward, I am not pleased with a reward for him less than Paradise. And this hadith, we do not recall it from Qatada, from Anas, except from this route."
"7223","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, how will people be gathered upon their faces on the Day of Resurrection? He said: The One Who made them walk upon their feet is able to make them walk upon their faces. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatada, from Anas, except Shayban."
"7224","And Ayyub ibn Sulayman al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: Malik ibn al-Dukhshum was mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they fell upon him, saying: He is the head of the hypocrites. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave my companions for me; do not revile my companions. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatada, from Anas, except Shayban, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Shayban except Adam."
"7225","Muhammad ibn Dawud al-Qantari, who is the brother of Ali ibn Dawud, narrated to us, Adam narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from madness, leprosy, vitiligo, sin, debt, deafness and dumbness; and I seek refuge in You from dying stung. Abu Bakr said: And he mentioned qualities I have forgotten. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatada, from Anas, except Shayban, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Shayban except Adam."
"7226","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Salim ibn Nuh narrated to us, Umar ibn Amir narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that Ukaydir of Duma sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a cloak of sundus, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore it, and people marveled at it, so he said: Do you marvel at this? By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, the handkerchiefs of Sad ibn Muadh in Paradise are better than it. Then he gifted it to Umar, who said: O Messenger of Allah, you dislike it while I wear it? He said: O Umar, I only sent it to you that you may send it to some direction and obtain wealth by it. He said: And that was before silk was forbidden."
"7227","Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari and al-Abbas ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Bakr and Umar: These two are the masters of the old men of the people of Paradise of the first and the last, except the prophets and messengers. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatada except al-Awzai, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from al-Awzai, from Qatada, from Anas, except Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Missisi."
"7228","Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abu al-Mughira Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Qatada, from Anas or another, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be in my nation disagreement and division: a people who speak well and do evil, reciting the Quran not passing their throats; one of you will belittle his prayer beside theirs and his fasting beside theirs; they pass through religion as the arrow passes through the game, then do not return until the arrow returns to its notch; they are the worst of creation; blessed is one who kills them and whom they kill; they call to the Book of Allah while they are of it in nothing; whoever kills them is worthier of Allah than them. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who are they that we may know them? He said: They are of our skin and speak with our tongues. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is their mark? He said: Shaving. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from the hadith of al-Awzai, from Qatada, from Anas."
"7229","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, al-Muthanna ibn Said narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not dye; there was only whiteness opposite the chin, or at the chin, little, in the temples little, and in the head little."
"7230","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, my father informed us, from al-Muthanna ibn Said, from Qatada, from Anas: that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raided, he said: O Allah, You are my support and my helper, and by You I fight. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatada, from Anas, except al-Muthanna ibn Said."
"7231","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Naji narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, al-Muthanna ibn Said narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed upon a mat. And this hadith, we do not recall it narrated from Qatada, from Anas, except from the hadith of al-Muthanna."
"7232","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid informed us, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Qatada ibn Diama: that Anas ibn Malik informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr and Asr, Maghrib and Isha, then slept a sleep at Mina, then rode to the House and circumambulated it. And we do not know Said ibn Abi Hilal narrated, from Qatada, from Anas, other than this hadith with a chain."
"7233","Uqba ibn Mukram al-Ammi narrated to us, Abu Qutayba narrated to us, Umar ibn Nabhan narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Differ from the Jews and pray in your socks and sandals, for they do not pray in their socks nor in their sandals. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Anas except from this route, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Umar ibn Nabhan except Abu Qutayba; Umar ibn Nabhan is well known."
"7234","Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman informed us, Umar ibn Nabhan narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I passed on the night I was taken by night by a people whose lips were clipped, so I said: Who are these? He said: These are the preachers of your nation, I think he said: Those who say what they do not do. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Qatada, from Anas, except by the narration of Umar ibn Nabhan, nor do we know from Umar except Jafar ibn Sulayman."
"7235","Talut ibn Abbad narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Ibrahim Abu Hatim narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Anas: that a man looked in upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while the Prophet, peace be upon him, had a stick, so he said: If I knew you were looking at me, I would have thrust it in your eyes, or similar to this."
"7236","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, Suwayd narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: A man reviled a flea before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Do not revile it, for it awakened a prophet of the prophets for the dawn prayer."
"7237","Al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Idris narrated to us, Suwayd narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved greenness, or he said: The most beloved of colors to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was greenness. And these three hadiths, we do not know anyone who narrates them from Qatada, from Anas, except Suwayd Abu Hatim, except that the hadith of the flea, they mentioned that Said ibn Bashir followed him upon it."
"7238","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Umayya ibn Khalid narrated to us, Ali ibn Masaada narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith is in the heart, while Islam is what is outward, or he said: open. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatada, from Anas, except Ali ibn Masaada."
"7239","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ali ibn Masaada Abu Habib al-Bahili narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All the sons of Adam err, and the best of those who err are the repentant. Abu Bakr said: And the two hadiths of Ali ibn Masaada, we do not know anyone who narrated them from Qatada, from Anas, other than him."
"7240","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, from his brother Khalid ibn Qays, from Qatada, from Anas: that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: How much prayer did Allah obligate upon His servants? He said: Five. He said: Is there anything before or after them? He said: Allah obligated upon His servants five prayers. So the man swore he would neither add to them nor decrease, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He succeeds if he is truthful, or: if he is truthful he will enter Paradise. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Anas except from this route."
"7241","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Nuh ibn Qays informed us, Khalid ibn Qays narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to Bakr ibn Wail: From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), to Bakr ibn Wail, that submit and you will be safe. But they found none to read it to them except a man of Banu Dubaya, so they are called Banu al-Katib. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except with this chain."
"7242","And with it: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to Kisra, Qaysar and every tyrant, calling them to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatada, from Anas, except Khalid ibn Qays."
"7243","Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, Nafi ibn Khalid al-Tahi narrated to us, Nuh ibn Qays al-Tahi narrated to us, from his brother Khalid ibn Qays, from Qatada, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Death will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, stood between Paradise and the Fire, then slaughtered. Then it will be said: O people of Paradise, eternity without death; and O people of the Fire, eternity without death. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Anas except from this route with this chain."
"7244","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, both said: Khalaf ibn Musa ibn Khalaf narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two rakas of Fajr: Say, O disbelievers, and: Say, He is Allah, One."
"7245","And with it: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed his companions one day when the sun had almost set, with only little of it remaining, and said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, what remains of the world compared to what passed of it is only like what remains of this day of yours compared to what passed of it; we see of the sun only little."
"7246","Ibn Muthanna narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Musa narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to admonish his companions, when three men passed by; one of them came and sat with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the second went a little then sat, while the third went on his way. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of these three? As for the one who came and sat with us, he turned, so Allah turned to him; as for the one who went a little then sat, he was shy, so Allah was shy of him; while the one who went on his way, he turned away, so Allah turned away from him."
"7247","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Mutahhar narrated to us, Musa ibn Khalaf narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That I sit with a people remembering Allah from the dawn prayer until the sun rises is more beloved to me than freeing four necks, I think he said, of the children of Ismail; and that I sit with a people remembering Allah from the Asr prayer until the sun sets is more beloved to me than freeing four necks, I think he said, of the children of Ismail. And these hadiths, we do not know anyone who narrated them from Qatada, from Anas, except Musa ibn Khalaf."
"7248","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, who said: Ahmad ibn Salih wrote to me, who said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Umar ibn al-Subh, from Qatada, from Anas: that on the day of Uhud, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered the group in one grave, advancing to the front of the grave the most reciting of them. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatada except Umar ibn al-Subh, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from him other than Ibn Jurayj, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Ibn Jurayj other than Ibn Wahb."
"7249","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hanan narrated to us, Baqiyya narrated to us, Utba ibn Abi Hakim narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rakas after witr, reciting in them: Say, O disbelievers, and: Say, He is Allah, One. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatada, from Anas, except Utba."
"7250","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, the wording being that of Abu Musa, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, from his father, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: I asked him about the recitation of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He used to extend his voice with elongation."
"7251","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas, he said: The hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was wavy hair, neither very curly nor very straight, reaching between his ears and his shoulders."
"7252","And with the same chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be cupped on the two jugular veins and the upper back."
"7253","And with the same chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had large feet and perspired greatly, and I never saw anything at all more beautiful than him."
"7254","And with the same chain he said: The pommel of the sword of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was of silver. And this hadith is only narrated from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn Abi al-Hasan, mursal."
"7255","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih wrote to me: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed 'aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn. And we do not know anyone who corroborated Jarir ibn Hazim in these hadiths."
"7256","Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When we are with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we see in ourselves what we love, but when we return to our families and mix with them we find ourselves changed; so they mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: If you were to remain as you are when you are with me in private, the angels would shake hands with you with their wings, but it is an hour and an hour. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Qatadah, from Anas, except Ma'mar."
"7257","And with the same chain he said: When the bier of Sa'd was carried, the hypocrites said: How light his bier is, and that was because of his judgment concerning Banu Qurayzah; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked, and he said: No, but the angels were carrying him."
"7258","And with the same chain: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was brought al-Buraq on the night I was taken by night, saddled and bridled, and it became refractory, so Jibril said to it: O Buraq, do you do this with Muhammad? No one more noble to Allah than him ever rode you; so it broke out in sweat."
"7259","And with the same chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sufficient for you among the women of the worlds are Maryam, Khadijah, Fatimah, and Asiyah."
"7260","And with the same chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped on the top of the foot because of a pain he had."
"7261","And with the same chain, and from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar, and the sons of the Ansar, and the sons of the sons of the Ansar."
"7262","And with the same chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be in my ummah dissension and division, and there will come a people who will impress you and who are impressed with themselves. And these hadiths which we mentioned from Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Anas, we do not know anyone who narrated them from Qatadah, from Anas, with this wording, other than Ma'mar, except the hadith: Forgive the Ansar, for Amr ibn Ali narrated it from Yazid ibn Zuray', from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas, and no one corroborated him in it."
"7263","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah and Humayd and Thabit, from Anas, he said: Prices rose in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so they said: O Messenger of Allah, prices have risen; will you not fix prices for us? He said: Indeed Allah, blessed and exalted, is the Creator, the Provider, the Fixer of prices."
"7264","Harun ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade squatting on the heels and sitting on one side with the leg out in prayer. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Salamah except Yahya ibn Ishaq, and it is not narrated from Anas except through this channel."
"7265","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit and Qatadah and Humayd, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Zuhr and 'Asr: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and: Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming."
"7266","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Khuza'i narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until people boast about mosques. And we do not know anyone who narrated these hadiths except Hammad ibn Salamah, except the hadith about the rise in prices, in which Hammam shared with him."
"7267","Ahmad ibn Jamil al-Marwazi and Muhammad ibn Abi Madh'ur narrated to us, both said: al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that a funeral passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he stood up for it, so it was said: O Messenger of Allah, it is the funeral of a Jew; so he said: I only stood for what is with it of angels, or: I only stood for the angels. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Qatadah other than Hammad ibn Salamah, and no one narrated it from Hammad except al-Nadr ibn Shumayl."
"7268","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no servant but that he has three close companions: as for one close companion, he says: What you spent is yours, and what you withheld is not yours, and that is his wealth; and as for one close companion, he says: I am with you, but when you come to the door of the king I leave you and return, and that is his family and his retinue; and one close companion says: I am with you wherever you enter and wherever you go out, and that is his deed; so he says: You were indeed the least significant of the three to me. These are his words, or their meaning. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Imran al-Qattan."
"7269","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out on a military expedition and left Ibn Umm Maktum behind to lead the people in prayer. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Imran al-Qattan."
"7270","Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-'Uruqi narrated to us: Shu'ayb ibn Bayan narrated to us: Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give one salutation of salam. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Imran al-Qattan, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Imran except Shu'ayb ibn Bayan, and Shu'ayb is weak in hadith; only what he alone narrates is written from his hadith."
"7271","And with the same chain: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke his fast with some people and said: The fasting people have broken their fast with you, and the righteous have eaten your food, and the angels have invoked blessings upon you. And Thabit has narrated this hadith from Anas."
"7272","And with the same chain: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Are you unable to be like Abu Damdam? They said: O Messenger of Allah, and who is Abu Damdam? He said: A man who, when morning came, would say: O Allah, I have given my honor in charity to whoever wronged me, or words to that effect."
"7273","And with the same chain: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by some people lifting a stone to square it, and said: What are these people doing? They said: They are squaring a stone, seeking strength; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not point you to one who is stronger than him - or words to that effect - the one among you who controls himself at the time of anger."
"7274","And with the same chain: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever gives up wine while he is able to have it, I shall surely give him to drink of it in the enclosure of sanctity, and whoever gives up silk while he is able to wear it, I shall surely clothe him with it in the enclosure of sanctity."
"7275","And with the same chain: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by some people wrestling, and said: What is this? They said: O Messenger of Allah, this is so-and-so the wrestler; no one wrestles him but he throws him down; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not point you to one who is stronger than him: a man whom another man wronged, so he swallowed his anger and overcame him, and overcame his devil and overcame his companion's devil."
"7276","Muhammad ibn al-Mu'ammal ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bilal narrated to us: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: Ramadan began, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This month has begun, and it is the blessed month of Allah; in it is a night: whoever is deprived of it has been deprived of good, and none is deprived of its good except every deprived one. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Imran, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Imran except Muhammad ibn Bilal."
"7277","Ibrahim ibn Hani' narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bakkar ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Bashir, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sovereignty is in Quraysh; they have a right over you, and you have a like right over them, so long as they judge justly, and when asked for mercy show mercy, and when they covenant fulfill; so whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."
"7278","Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Himsi narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he wanted to sleep, would say: O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the day You resurrect Your servants. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Qatadah, from Anas, except Sa'id ibn Bashir."
"7279","Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck the parable of man, the appointed term, and hope, saying: The parable of the appointed term is at his side and hope is before him; while he hopes for what is before him, his appointed term comes to him and snatches him away."
"7280","Yahya ibn al-Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us: Yahya ibn Salih narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Change gray hair, or he said: The best thing with which you change gray hair is henna and katam. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Qatadah, from Anas, except Sa'id ibn Bashir."
"7281","Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When supper and prayer are both present, begin with supper."
"7282","Muhammad ibn Sudran narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Atiyyah narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Qatadah, from Anas, except Yusuf ibn Atiyyah, and Yusuf was not strong; only what is not preserved from others is written from his hadith."
"7283","Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Muharrar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Everything has an adornment, and the adornment of the Qur'an is a beautiful voice."
"7284","Suhayl ibn Ibrahim al-Jarudi Abu al-Khattab narrated to us: Awf ibn Muhammad al-Murari narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Muharrar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed 'aqiqah for himself after he was sent as a prophet. And the two hadiths of Abdullah ibn Muharrar, we do not know anyone who narrated them from Qatadah, from Anas, other than him, and he is very weak in hadith; only what is not found with others is written from his hadith."
"7285","Isma'il ibn Abdullah narrated to us: Qutaybah narrated to us: Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Salih, from Harun, from Muqatil ibn Hayyan, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Everything has a heart, and the heart of the Qur'an is Ya-Sin."
"7286","Muhammad ibn Salih al-Adawi narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf married a woman in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for the weight of a date-stone of gold; he said: its value was three dirhams and a third. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Qatadah, from Anas, except al-Hajjaj ibn Artah."
"7287","Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us: Hafs ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has pardoned for my ummah what their souls whisper, so long as they do not speak of it or act upon it. And al-Hajjaj ibn Artah and Hafs ibn Abd al-Rahman have contradicted the firmly established narrations from Qatadah in this hadith, so I do not know whether it is from Hafs or from al-Hajjaj; for Shu'bah, Sa'id, and Mis'ar narrate this hadith from Qatadah, from Zurarah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7288","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bazi' narrated to us: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Marzuq ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrating from his Lord, He said: The mujahid is guaranteed by Me: if I take him or return him, and if I return him, I return him with reward and spoils."
"7289","Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Bishr narrated to us: al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded with the Pledge of Ridwan, Uthman ibn Affan was the messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to the people of Makkah, so the people gave pledge; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, Uthman is attending to Your need and the need of Your Messenger; so he struck one of his hands upon the other, and the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on behalf of Uthman was better for him than their own hands were for themselves."
"7290","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us: Shabbabah narrated to us: al-Mughirah ibn Muslim narrated to us: Matar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking while standing, and eating while standing, and eating the animal tied up as a target, and the jallalah animal, and drinking from the mouth of the waterskin. Al-Mughirah ibn Muslim is righteous, and parts of the wording of this hadith are narrated from Qatadah, from Anas, and part of it from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas."
"7291","Muhammad ibn Mirdas al-Ansari narrated to us: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us: Abbad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: While I was passing the cup around to Abu Talhah, Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, Mu'adh ibn Jabal, Suhayl ibn Bayda', and Abu Dujanah, until their heads began to nod, we heard a caller calling: Wine has indeed been forbidden; so no one entered upon us and none of us went out, and we poured out the drink, broke the jars, some of us performed ablution and some bathed, and we applied some of the perfume of Umm Sulaym; then we went out to the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was reciting: O you who believe, wine, gambling, idols, and divining arrows are but filth from the work of Satan, until he reached: Will you then desist. So a man said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the standing of one who died while drinking it? So Allah, blessed and exalted, revealed: There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they tasted - the verse. Then a man said to Qatadah: Did you hear it from Anas? He said: Yes. And a man said to Anas: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes - or: one who would not lie to me narrated to me - for by Allah, we never used to lie, nor did we know what lying was. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Abbad ibn Rashid, a well-known man of Basra."
"7292","Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Hani' narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah al-Arzami narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seven things whose reward continues for the servant after his death while he is in his grave: one who taught knowledge, or dug a canal, or dug a well, or planted a palm tree, or built a mosque, or bequeathed a mushaf, or left a child who seeks forgiveness for him after his death."
"7293","Al-Husayn ibn al-Aswad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he used to stand in prayer until his feet swelled, so it was said to him: Do you do that though Allah has forgiven you what preceded of your sin and what followed? He said: Shall I not be a grateful servant. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Bishr, from Mis'ar, from Qatadah, from Anas, except Abdullah ibn Awn al-Kharraz and al-Husayn ibn al-Aswad; others narrate it from Muhammad ibn Bishr, from Mis'ar, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, and that is the correct version."
"7294","Amr ibn Abdillah al-Awdi narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prophet has a supplication he made, and I have kept my supplication hidden as intercession for my ummah."
"7295","Ja'far ibn Muhammad, nephew of Waki', narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that he forbade continuous fasting, so it was said: O Messenger of Allah, you fast continuously; he said: I spend the night with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink."
"7296","Muhammad ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: Ayyub ibn Utbah narrated to us, from al-Fadl ibn Bakr, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things are destructive: obeyed miserliness, followed desire, and a man's admiration of his own opinion. And no one narrated this hadith from Qatadah, from Anas, except al-Fadl ibn Bakr, and no one narrated from al-Fadl except Ayyub ibn Utbah."
"7297","Al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Rukhami narrated to us: Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Which creation has the most amazing faith? They said: The angels; he said: The angels, how could they not believe? He said: The prophets; he said: Revelation comes to the prophets, so how could they not believe? They said: The Companions; he said: The Companions are with the prophets, so how could they not believe; but the people with the most amazing faith are a people who come after you and find a book of revelation, so they believe in it and follow it; they are the most amazing of people - or of creation - in faith. It is strange as a hadith of Anas."
"7298","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan al-Wasiti narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Ziyad ibn Ubaydillah narrated to us: Shayban Abu Mu'awiyah, and he is Abu Abd al-Rahman, narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever seeks knowledge to boast with it before scholars, or to argue with it against fools, or to turn people's faces toward him, is in the Fire. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Anas except with this chain, and no one narrated it from Shayban except this Sulayman ibn Ziyad. More than one narrated it from him, and he was not corroborated in this narration; Shayban is trustworthy, and Sulayman ibn Ziyad has been narrated from by more than one of the people of knowledge, though he was not corroborated in this hadith. The sixth juz' is complete, by the praise of Allah."
"7299","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, both said: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Musa ibn Anas, from Anas: that a Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he ordered for him sheep filling the space between two mountains; so he came to his people and said: O my people, accept Islam, for Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gives a giving that does not fear poverty. And we do not know this hadith narrated except from Anas, and we do not know a better chain for it from Anas than this chain."
"7300","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Musa ibn Anas, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You left behind in Madinah men: you did not cross a valley nor travel any distance but they were with you; they said: O Messenger of Allah, how, while they are in Madinah? He said: Excuse kept them back. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Humayd, from Musa ibn Anas, from Anas, except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"7301","Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari and Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, both said: Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us: Ibn Abi Uways, meaning Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways, narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal - Ibn Shabib said: from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Humayd, from Musa ibn Anas, from Anas; Abu Bakr said: I did not find in my book from al-Bukhari except from Sulayman, from Humayd, from Musa ibn Anas, from Anas - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held a wedding feast for Safiyyah. And we do not know that Humayd narrated with a chain from Musa ibn Anas, from Anas, except these three hadiths."
"7302","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: Musa ibn Anas narrated to us, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."
"7303","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Abbas and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, the wording being Muhammad ibn Ma'mar's, both said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Anas, from Anas: that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Who is my father? He said: Your father is so-and-so; he said: And there was revealed: O you who believe, do not ask about things which, if made plain to you, would trouble you; so Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, stood and said: We are pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as prophet; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise and Hell were shown to me, and I never saw, in good and evil, the like of today."
"7304","And Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to us: al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Anas, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise and Hell were shown to me, and I never saw, in good and evil, the like of today; and if you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much; so a man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, who is my father? He said: Your father is so-and-so; so Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, stood and said: We are pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as prophet. He said: And this verse was revealed: O you who believe, do not ask about things which, if made plain to you, would trouble you. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except al-Nadr ibn Shumayl and Rawh ibn Ubadah, from Shu'bah."
"7305","Harun ibn Sufyan al-Mustamli and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abd al-Karim al-Azdi narrated to us, both said: Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Anas, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Shu'bah except Aswad ibn Amir, and we do not know that Shu'bah narrated with a chain from Musa ibn Anas, from Anas, except these three hadiths."
"7306","Nasr ibn Ali informed us: Abu Ahmad narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Mukhtar, from Musa ibn Anas, from Anas, he said: I prayed, I and Abu Talhah, behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with Umm Sulaym behind us. And Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah has narrated this hadith from Anas, and we do not know it narrated from Musa ibn Anas, from Anas, except through this channel we mentioned."
"7307","Nasr ibn Ali informed us: Abu Ahmad narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us - or Shayban - from Abdullah ibn al-Mukhtar, from Musa ibn Anas, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a small box of perfume with which he perfumed himself. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Anas except through this channel."
"7308","Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to us, he said: I heard Musa ibn Anas narrating from Anas: that irrigation channels were hard upon the Ansar, so they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to supplicate for them; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed of that and said: You will not ask me for anything today but I shall give it to you; so when they heard what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, they said: Supplicate to Allah for us; he said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar, and the sons of the Ansar, and the sons of the sons of the Ansar. And this hadith has been narrated from Anas through more than one channel with different wordings, and we do not know it narrated from Musa ibn Anas except in the hadith of Abdullah ibn Abi Yazid."
"7309","From the hadith of al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Harb ibn Maymun narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, said: When I take the sight of My servant and he is patient over it, I compensate My servant with Paradise. And this hadith has been narrated from Anas and from others than Anas with a different wording, and we do not know for al-Nadr ibn Anas any chain except this chain."
"7310","And with the same chain he said: I pledged to meet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I asked him to intercede for me, and he said: I shall do so."
"7311","And with the same chain he said: I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a funeral passed, so he said: What is this funeral? They said: The funeral of so-and-so son of so-and-so; he used to love Allah and His Messenger; he said: It has become due, three times; then another passed, so he said: What is this? They said: The funeral of so-and-so son of so-and-so; he used to hate Allah and His Messenger; so he said: It has become due, three times."
"7312","And with the same chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar and the sons of the Ansar; the Ansar are my inner garment and my receptacle; and if people were to take - I think he said - a mountain pass, and the Ansar took a mountain pass, I would take their pass; and were it not for the Hijrah, I would be a man of the Ansar."
"7313","Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Harb ibn Maymun narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, he said: Umm Sulaym came to the father of Anas and said: I have come today with what you dislike; so he said: You keep coming with what I dislike from that Bedouin - he was a Bedouin whom Allah chose, selected, and made a prophet - he said: What have you brought? She said: Wine has been forbidden; this is separation between me and you; so he died a polytheist. And Abu Talhah came to Umm Sulaym and said: What brings you, O Abu Talhah? He said: I have come as a suitor; she said: Have you accepted Islam? He said: No; he said: What do you ask about my Islam? She said: I would not marry you while you are a polytheist; he said: No, by Allah, this is not your habit; she said: What is my habit? He said: Your habit is in yellow and white metal; she said: I call you to witness, and I call the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to witness, that if you accept Islam, I am content with Islam from you as dowry; he said: Who will arrange this for me? She said: O Anas, stand and go with your uncle; so he stood and placed his hand on my shoulder, and we went until we were near the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he heard his speech and said: This is Abu Talhah; between his eyes is the radiance of Islam; until he came and greeted the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married him to her for Islam. She bore him a boy, then the boy grew and his father was delighted with him, then Allah, blessed and exalted, took him to Himself. Abu Talhah came and said: How is my son, O Umm Sulaym? She said: The best he ever was; she said: Will you not have lunch? You have delayed your lunch today; so she brought his lunch near, and he ate lunch until he was full, then she adorned herself for him as she had never adorned herself before, then they were together, and when she saw that he was satisfied and had eaten, she said: O Abu Talhah, what do you think about people who deposited something with some people, then its owners sought it back - would they have the right to prevent it? He said: No; she said: Then seek reward in your son, for Allah took him; so he became angry and said: You left me until I ate and was together with you, then you told me of my son; so he went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him what had happened, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah bless you two in your night; so she became pregnant, and when the time of her delivery approached, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and she was with him, and he would not return from a journey and enter Madinah at night; when they drew near Madinah, labor seized her, and Abu Talhah stayed with her while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went on; Abu Talhah said: O Lord, You know that I love to go out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he goes out, and to enter with him when he enters, and I have been detained as You see; Umm Sulaym said: O Abu Talhah, I no longer feel what I felt, so let us go on; so they went on, and when they entered Madinah, labor seized her again and she gave birth to a boy; my mother said to me: O Anas, let no one feed him until you take him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the morning; when morning came, I carried him and went with him to him, and I found him with a branding iron branding the camels of sadaqah; when he saw me he said: Perhaps Umm Sulaym has given birth; I said: Yes; so he put down the iron, I brought him near, he chewed a date and rubbed his palate with it and named him Abdullah. And we do not know this hadith narrated from al-Nadr ibn Anas except through Harb ibn Maymun."
"7314","The hadith of Thumamah ibn Abdullah ibn Anas, from Anas: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us, both said: Azhar ibn Sa'd narrated to us: Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Thumamah ibn Abdullah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the house of a tailor boy, so he brought near to him a bowl containing tharid with pumpkin on it; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to pick out the pumpkin, and I have loved pumpkin ever since that day."
"7315","And Salamah ibn Shabib narrated it to us: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar informed us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"7316","And Ali ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us: Nasr ibn Hammad narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah and Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to like pumpkin. And the hadith of Ibn Awn, from Thumamah, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Azhar; and the hadith of Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Nasr ibn Hammad, from Shu'bah, combining in it Qatadah and Mu'awiyah; it is only known from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Ghundar and others - and Nasr is lenient in hadith - and the hadith of Asim al-Ahwal, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Ma'mar, from Asim."
"7317","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna al-Ansari narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Thumamah, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit Umm Sulaym and take his midday rest with her on a leather mat; when he slept, she would take some of his sweat and put it in bottles, and put it in her perfume box."
"7318","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Thumamah, from Anas: that the ring of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with Abu Bakr and Umar, and with Uthman for six years, acting like their practice, may Allah be pleased with them; and its inscription was three lines: Muhammad one line, Messenger one line, and Allah one line."
"7319","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from Thumamah, from Anas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Makkah, Qays was in his vanguard, so Sa'd spoke to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to move him from the position he was in, fearing he would undertake something, so he moved him from that."
"7320","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated it to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Thumamah, from Anas: that Qays ibn Sa'd was to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the position of the chief of police to the commander."
"7321","Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Azrah ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Thumamah, from Anas: that he used to breathe in the vessel three times; and Anas mentioned that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to breathe in the vessel three times."
"7322","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Azrah, meaning Ibn Thabit, narrated to us, from Thumamah, from Anas: that he would not refuse perfume; and Anas said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Do not refuse perfume."
"7323","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Abu Qutaybah narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, from Thumamah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he spoke a word, would repeat it three times, and when he came to people and greeted them, he would greet them three times."
"7324","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna, from Thumamah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"7325","Abu Khallad Sulayman ibn Khallad narrated to us: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, from Thumamah, from Anas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked in the mirror, he would say: Praise be to Allah who fashioned my creation and made my form good, and adorned of me what He disfigured of others. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel with this chain, and Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar was not a memorizer."
"7326","Ziyad ibn Yahya and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, both said: Abu Attab Sahl ibn Hammad narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, from Thumamah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a fly falls into the vessel of one of you, let him dip it, for in one of its wings is disease and in the other is cure. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Anas except through this channel with this chain."
"7327","Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Idris narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, from Thumamah, from Anas, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Umm Sulaym gave birth to her child, and I found with him a branding iron with which he branded the camels of sadaqah; so he rubbed his palate and named him Abdullah."
"7328","And with the same chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"7329","Al-Walid ibn Umar ibn Sukayn narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, from his father, from Thumamah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Hunayn: Cut them down, and he gestured with his hand toward the throat. And these words, we do not know anyone who narrated them except Anas, and we do not know any chain for them from Anas except this chain."
"7330","Al-Walid ibn Amr ibn Sukayn narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, from his father, from Thumamah, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to our house, so we gave him to drink from a well of ours in our house that was called al-Burur in the pre-Islamic period; he drank his fill from it, and it never ran dry afterward. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Anas, and we do not know any chain for it from Anas except this chain."
"7331","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Adi, nephew of al-Husayn ibn Adi, narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, from his father, from Thumamah, from Anas: that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, if I am killed in the path of Allah, patient and seeking reward, shall I enter Paradise? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes; then when he turned away he said: Except debt. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Anas except through this channel, and we heard it only from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Adi, and he was, Allah willing, among the righteous."
"7332","Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr narrated to us: Hatim ibn Ubaydillah al-Attar narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, from Thumamah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man following a pigeon and said: A devil following a devil. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Anas except through this channel."
"7333","Al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us: Yahya ibn Maymun Abu Ayyub al-Tammar narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, from his grandfather, meaning Thumamah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dye with henna, for it increases your youthfulness and your marital vigor. And this hadith was narrated only by Yahya ibn Maymun, and he was not corroborated in it."
"7334","Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr narrated to us: Hatim narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, from Thumamah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took off his sandals in prayer. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Anas except through this channel."
"7335","Bishr ibn Adam, son of the daughter of Azhar, narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Thumamah, from Anas, he said: When this verse was revealed: You will never attain righteousness until you spend of what you love - or: Who is it that will lend Allah a good loan - Abu Talhah came and said: O Messenger of Allah, my walled garden is for Allah, and if I could conceal it I would not make it public; he said: Put it among your poor family, or your relatives; so he gave it to Hassan ibn Thabit and Ubayy."
"7336","And with the same chain he said: We had a cup, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would come to the house of Umm Sulaym and sit on her leather mat, eat of her food, drink from the cup, and she would take his sweat and put it in her perfume box."
"7337","Muhammad ibn Mirdas narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Awf, from Thumamah, from Anas - thus I found it in my book in my handwriting, from Thumamah, from Anas - and others said: from Thumamah ibn Abdullah ibn Anas; and we do not know anyone who said: from Ibn Abi Adi, from Awf, from Thumamah, from Anas, except a man called Musa ibn Hayyan, whose word is not adduced as proof; and Muhammad ibn Mirdas is unobjectionable, truthful; so I saw it in my book in my handwriting from Ibn Abi Adi, from Awf, from Thumamah, from Anas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah, the slave girls of the Ansar met him and began saying: [the transmitted text ends here]."
"7338","Abdah ibn Abdullah narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Jamil ibn Ubayd Abu al-Nadr narrated to us: Thumamah narrated to us, from his grandfather Anas ibn Malik, he said: The caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said: The qiblah has been turned, while the imam was in prayer having prayed two rak'ahs; the caller said: The qiblah has been turned toward the Ka'bah, so pray the remaining two rak'ahs toward the Ka'bah. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Thumamah except Jamil ibn Ubayd."
"7339","Abdah ibn Abdullah narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Jamil ibn Ubayd Abu al-Nadr narrated to us: Thumamah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from his grandfather Anas, he said: I was serving them drink, then a caller came to us and said: Wine has been forbidden; so I poured it out, and it was at that time fadikh. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Thumamah except Jamil."
"7340","Abdah ibn Abdullah narrated to us: Zayd narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Thumamah, from Anas, he said: Four gathered the Qur'an in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Ubayy ibn Ka'b, Zayd ibn Thabit, Mu'adh ibn Jabal, and Abu Zayd."
"7341","He said: Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi wrote to me, mentioning that Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to him, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna, from Thumamah, from Anas, he said: There was a camel-driver driving with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Gently, driving the glass vessels."
"7342","Abdullah ibn al-Sabbah al-Attar narrated to us: al-Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us: Abu Bakr al-Hudhali narrated to us, from Thumamah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees something he likes and says: What Allah willed, there is no power except with Allah, it will not harm him. And these words, we do not know anyone who narrated them except Anas, and we do not know any chain for them except this chain."
"7343","I found in my book, from Abu Hisham: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, meaning al-Sa'di, from Thumamah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer between graves."
"7344","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, both said: Abu Asim narrated to us: Mubarak al-Khayyat narrated to us, he said: I asked Thumamah about coitus interruptus, so he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about coitus interruptus, so he said: If the fluid from which a child comes were cast upon a rock, Allah would bring forth a child from it, and Allah will surely create every soul He is to create. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Anas except through this channel with this chain."
"7345","Sa'dan ibn Yazid narrated to us: al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, from Thumamah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a donkey branded on its face and said: Allah curse whoever did this."
"7346","I found in my book, from Amr ibn Malik, from Yazid ibn Zuray', from Hisham, from Azrah ibn Thabit, from Thumamah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj on a worn saddle with a striped cloak under it, and said: A Hajj with no showing off in it and no seeking of repute. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Yazid ibn Zuray', from Hisham al-Dastuwa'i."
"7347","The hadith of Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: O Allah, there is no life but the life of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirah."
"7348","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The son of the sister of a people is of them."
"7349","Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us: Abu Zayd Sa'id ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas - I think he raised it - he said: The parable of a good word, he said: it is the palm tree; and the parable of an evil word as an evil tree, he said: it is the shiryan tree."
"7350","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas, similarly, and he did not raise it."
"7351","Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Azraq narrated to us: Yahya ibn al-Sakan narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah and Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No soul that dies having good with Allah loves to return to this world except the martyr. And we do not know anyone who combined Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah and Qatadah in it except Yahya ibn al-Sakan, from Shu'bah; it is only known from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Anas; and we do not know that Shu'bah narrated with a chain from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas, except five hadiths."
"7352","Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us: Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every ummah has a monasticism, and the monasticism of this ummah is jihad in the path of Allah. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith with a chain except Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham, from Sufyan; others than Mu'awiyah narrate it mursal."
"7353","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas, raising it, he said: Supplication between the adhan and the iqamah is not rejected."
"7354","Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: al-Jald ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas, that he said: We have not seen the like of what has reached us from our Lord, blessed and exalted, then we did not go out to Him devoid of all family and wealth: that He pardoned us for what is less than major sins; Allah, blessed and exalted, says: If you avoid the major sins of what you are forbidden, We shall expiate your evil deeds and admit you to a noble entrance."
"7355","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Khulayd ibn Ja'far, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas, he said: Allah did not disfigure him with gray hair, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7356","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us: Hassan ibn Ibrahim al-Kirmani narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Masruq narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, he said: Anas said: I do not recognize anything of what we were upon, meaning except this, except prayer. And we do not know that Sa'id ibn Masruq narrated from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah any hadith entering the Musnad except this hadith, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Sa'id ibn Masruq except Hassan."
"7357","Al-Harith ibn al-Khidr al-Attar narrated to us: Uthman ibn Farqad al-Attar narrated to us: Jald ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas, raising it, he said: Three things are of disrespect: that a man blow in his prostration, or wipe his forehead before finishing his prayer, and the third has slipped my mind - Abu Bakr said."
"7358","Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us: Ya'mar ibn Bishr narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Imran ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never seen putting his knee forward before a sitting companion of his, nor did he shake hands with a man and withdraw his hand from his hand until the man was the one who withdrew it. And others than Ibn al-Mubarak narrated this hadith from Imran, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Anas, without mentioning Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah."
"7359","The hadith of Amr ibn Sa'id, from Anas: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: al-Mughirah ibn Salamah narrated to us: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Amr ibn Sa'id, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the most merciful of people to children."
"7360","And Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated it to us: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Amr ibn Sa'id, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly. And a group narrated this hadith from Ayyub, from Anas, without mentioning Amr ibn Sa'id, except Wuhayb and Ibn Ulayyah."
"7361","Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us: Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Amr ibn Sa'id, from Anas, he said: I was riding behind Abu Talhah on the day we came to Khaybar, with hoes in their hands bringing water; when they saw us they threw down what was in their hands and said: Muhammad and the army; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Greatest, Khaybar is ruined; when we descend in the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those warned. And Amr ibn Sa'id is a man of Basra; Ayyub, Yunus, Ibn Awn, and Dawud narrated from him."
"7362","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Ashhal ibn Hatim narrated to us: Ibn Awn said, from Amr ibn Sa'id, from Anas, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he came to the door of a woman he had newly married; there were people with her, so he went away, attended to his need, and delayed; then he returned and there were people with her, so he went away, attended to his need, returned, and they had gone out; so he entered and let down a curtain between me and him; I mentioned it to Abu Talhah, so he said: If it is as you say, something must have been revealed about this; so the verse of hijab was revealed. The hadith of Hanzalah al-Sadusi, from Anas."
"7363","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Abd al-A'la ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Hanzalah, from Anas, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, should some of us bow to others when we meet? He said: No; it was said: Should some of us embrace others? He said: No; he said: Should we shake hands? He said: Shake hands."
"7364","And Muhammad ibn Musa narrated it to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hanzalah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"7365","And Taliq ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated it to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Shu'bah informed us, from Hanzalah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to the hadith of Hisham, from Hanzalah, from Anas. And we do not know anyone who narrated these words except Hanzalah, from Anas; we mentioned it only because his hadith is with this hadith; and we do not know anyone who narrated the hadith of Shu'bah, from Hanzalah, except Yazid ibn Harun."
"7366","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hanzalah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut in the Fajr prayer, and I memorized of his supplication: Make their hearts like the hearts of disbelieving women. And we do not know this hadith narrated with this wording from Anas except in the hadith of Hanzalah."
"7367","Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam al-Ijli narrated to us: Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami narrated to us, from Hanzalah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to add, to the People of the Book, more than: And upon you. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Hanzalah, from Anas, except Umar ibn Ali."
"7368","Abu al-Khattab Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Abu Bahr Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Hanzalah al-Sadusi, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Umm Mubashshir when she had planted a planting, and said: No Muslim plants a planting or sows a crop from which a bird, beast, or man eats, but he has reward in it. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Hanzalah except Abu Bahr."
"7369","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Muslim narrated to us: al-Harith ibn Nabhan narrated to us: Hanzalah al-Sadusi narrated to us, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he forbade nabidh of jars, and keeping sacrificial meats beyond three days, and visiting graves; then he said: I had forbidden you nabidh of jars, so make nabidh in whatever seems good to you, for a vessel neither makes anything lawful nor unlawful; and I had forbidden you keeping sacrificial meats beyond three days, so keep them as seems good to you; and I had forbidden you visiting graves, so visit them, for they remind of the Hereafter. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Hanzalah except al-Harith."
"7370","The hadith of Marwan al-Asfar, from Anas: Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us: Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Salim ibn Hayyan, trustworthy, narrated to us, from Marwan al-Asfar, from Anas. And Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad narrated it to us: my father narrated to us: Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Marwan al-Asfar, from Anas: that Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Yemen, so he said to him: With what did you enter ihram? He said: I entered ihram with what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram with; so he said: Were it not that the sacrificial animal is with me, I would have exited ihram. And we do not know that Marwan al-Asfar narrated with a chain from Anas except this hadith."
"7371","Yazid ibn Dirham, from Anas: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Idris narrated to us: Awn ibn Kahmas narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Dirham, from Anas, he said: I heard Anas saying concerning this verse: We sufficed you against the mockers, who set up another god with Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by, and some of them winked; then Jibril came - I think he said - and winked at them, and there fell upon their bodies like the mark of a stab, until they died. And we do not know that Yazid ibn Dirham narrated with a chain from Anas except this hadith, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Anas other than him."
"7372","Budayl ibn Maysarah, from Anas: Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Budayl ibn Maysarah narrated to us, from his father, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has people of His household among people; it was said: O Messenger of Allah, who are they? He said: They are the people of the Qur'an; they are the people of Allah and His elite. And we do not know anyone who narrates this hadith except Budayl ibn Maysarah, from Anas."
"7373","And Abdah ibn Abdullah narrated to us: Abd al-Samad narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to us, from Budayl ibn Maysarah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two traits may not be withheld: water and fire. And we do not know this hadith narrated except from Anas through this channel, and we do not know that Budayl narrated with a chain from Anas except these two hadiths. Ata' ibn Abi Maymunah, from Anas."
"7374","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ata' ibn Abi Maymunah: that he heard Anas ibn Malik say: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the lavatory, a boy would follow him with a small water vessel, and he would cleanse himself with water."
"7375","Al-Walid ibn Amr ibn Sukayn narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani narrated to us, from Ata' ibn Abi Maymunah, from Anas, he said: Nothing involving retaliation was ever brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but he commanded pardon in it. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Anas except with this chain."
"7376","Muhammad ibn Mirdas narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Atiyyah narrated to us: Ata' ibn Abi Maymunah narrated to us, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Patience is at the first shock. And Shu'bah has narrated this hadith from Thabit, from Anas; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ata' ibn Abi Maymunah except Yusuf ibn Atiyyah, though people accepted his hadith."
"7377","Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hear and obey, even if an Abyssinian slave whose head is like a raisin is put in authority over you."
"7378","And Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated it to us: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly. And we do not know anyone who narrated these words except Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas, and the name of Abu al-Tayyah is Yazid ibn Humayd."
"7379","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make things easy and do not make them hard, give calm and do not drive away."
"7380","And with the same chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray in sheepfolds before the house was built."
"7381","And Yahya ibn Habib narrated it to us: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas."
"7382","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Abu al-Walid narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Ansar said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: He gives to Quraysh; this is indeed astonishing: our swords drip with the blood of Quraysh, yet our spoils are returned to them; that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he called the Ansar specifically and said: What is it that reached me about you? And they would not lie; they said: It is what reached you; so he said: Are you not pleased that people go to their houses with spoils while you return to your houses with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the Ansar were to take a valley or a mountain pass, I would take the valley of the Ansar, or their mountain pass."
"7383","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Blessing is in the forelocks of horses."
"7384","And Yahya ibn Habib narrated it to us: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"7385","Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Anas: Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us: al-Firyabi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted ruqyah for the evil eye and venomous stings."
"7386","Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Anas: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bazi', and Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated to us, they said: Ziyad ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us: Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, from Anas, he said: I do not recognize today anything of what we were upon in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); they said: O Abu Hamzah, what about prayer? He said: Did you not do in prayer what you know."
"7387","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated to us, both said: Ziyad ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us: Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: I liken people today, and the multitude of wide cloaks in the mosque, only to the Jews of Khaybar. Ziyad ibn al-Rabi' alone narrated both."
"7388","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit and Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Some will come out of the Fire - Abu Imran said: four, and Thabit said: two men - so they are presented before Allah, then they are ordered to the Fire; one of them turns and says: I had hoped in You, when You took me out of it, that You would not return me to it; so Allah, blessed and exalted, saves him from it."
"7389","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Abu Imran al-Jawni; and Azhar ibn Jamil narrated it to us: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah says to the lightest of the people of the Fire in punishment on the Day of Resurrection: If you had all that is on earth, would you ransom yourself with it? He says: Yes; so He says to him: I wanted of you what is easier than that, when you were - I think he said - in the loins of your father Adam, or the loins of Adam: that you not associate anything with Me, but you refused except to associate with Me. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Anas, except Shu'bah."
"7390","Bishr ibn Hilal al-Sawwaf narrated to us: Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Duba'i narrated to us: Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, from Anas, he said: A time was fixed for us in trimming the mustache, clipping nails, plucking the armpit, and shaving the pubic hair: forty days. And we do not know anyone well-known who narrated this hadith from Anas except Abu Imran al-Jawni, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Anas; and Sadaqah ibn Musa said in it, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed a time for us, then he mentioned similarly."
"7391","Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us: al-Harith ibn Ghassan narrated to us: Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The deeds of the sons of Adam are presented before Allah on the Day of Resurrection in sealed scrolls, so Allah says: Cast this away, and accept this; the angels say: O Lord, by Allah, we saw of him only good; so Allah says: His deed was for other than My sake, and I accept today of deeds only what was intended for My sake. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Anas except through this channel; al-Harith ibn Ghassan is a man of Basra, unobjectionable; a group of the people of knowledge narrated from him."
"7392","Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us: al-Harith ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While I was sitting, Jibril, peace be upon him, came and nudged me between my shoulders; so I stood toward a tree in which were like two birds' nests; he sat in one of them and I sat in the other; it rose and ascended until it blocked the two horizons, while I turned my gaze; had I wished to touch the sky I would have touched it; Jibril turned to me as though he were a worn mat lying flat, so I recognized the superiority of his knowledge of Allah over mine; a door of the gates of heaven was opened for me, I saw the greatest light, and beneath the veil was the fluttering of pearls and rubies; so He revealed to me what He willed to reveal. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Anas, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Imran except al-Harith ibn Ubayd, a well-known man of Basra."
"7393","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us: Muslim informed us: al-Harith ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by children and greeted them. And Thabit has narrated this hadith from Anas, and we do not know it narrated in the hadith of Abu Imran except from al-Harith ibn Ubayd, from him."
"7394","Isma'il ibn Abi al-Harith al-Baghdadi narrated to us: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us: Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to breathe in the vessel three times."
"7395","And Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated it to us: Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id informed us: Abu Isam narrated to us, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to breathe in the vessel three times, and would say: It is more pleasant, more wholesome, and healthier. And the hadith of Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Anas, was narrated from Abu Imran only by Salih al-Murri."
"7396","7393 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, Ghassan ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you lay your side on the bed and recite the Opening of the Book (al-Fatiha) and Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad, you are safe from everything except death. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated with this wording except from Anas through this route, and we heard it only from Ibrahim ibn Sa'id."
"7397","7394 - I heard Amr ibn Ali saying: I heard Abu Qutaybah saying, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray in his sandals. Amr ibn Ali said: So I said to Abu Qutaybah, it is only from Abu Maslamah, and he said: This is how I memorized it."
"7398","7395 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Maslamah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with something similar. And it (the latter) is the correct one, and Abu Qutaybah erred in it."
"7399","7396 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Uwayd ibn Abi Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised me with five qualities, he said: O Anas, perform ablution fully, your lifespan will be increased; and greet whomever you meet of my ummah, your good deeds will multiply; and when you enter - meaning your house - greet your household, the good of your house will increase; and pray the Duha prayer, for it is the prayer of the penitent before you; O Anas, show mercy to the young and honor the elder, you will be among my companions on the Day of Resurrection. The hadith of Hisham ibn Zayd, from Anas."
"7400","7397 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Mu'adh narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd, from Anas, he said: When the day of Hunayn came, Hawazin and Ghatafan advanced, and with them were their riding animals and livestock, and with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that day were ten thousand men, and with him were the freed ones (Tulaqa). They turned away from him until he remained alone. He then called out that day two calls with nothing mixed between them: he turned to his right and said: O company of the Ansar, and they said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah, we are with you; and he turned to his left and said: O company of the Ansar, they said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah, we are with you. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a white mule. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended and said: I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger. The polytheists were defeated, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) acquired many spoils, and he distributed them among the Muhajirun and the Tulaqa and did not give the Ansar anything. The Ansar said: When there is hardship we are called, and the spoils are given to others. That reached him, so he gathered them in a tent and said: O company of the Ansar, what is this report that reached me? They fell silent. He said: O company of the Ansar, are you not pleased that the people go with worldly things and you go with Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to your houses? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, we are pleased. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the people take a valley and the Ansar take a mountain path, I would take the mountain path of the Ansar. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Hisham ibn Zayd, from Anas, except Ibn Awn."
"7401","7398 - Yahya ibn Habib ibn Adi narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd, from Anas; that a Jewish woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a poisoned sheep, and he ate from it. She was brought, and it was said: Shall we not kill her, or shall we kill her? He said: No. He said: I continued to recognize it (its effect) in the uvula of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7402","7399 - And al-Sakan ibn Sa'id narrated it to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. And we do not know anyone narrated this hadith from Shu'bah except Khalid ibn al-Harith and Rawh."
"7403","7400 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, they said, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd, from Anas, he said: We passed by and startled a rabbit at Marr al-Zahran, and we pursued it until we caught it. I brought it to Abu Talhah, so he slaughtered it and sent its haunch and thigh to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I brought them to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he accepted them. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Anas except Hisham ibn Zayd, and more than one narrated it from Hushaym: Shu'bah, and Ash'ath, and others."
"7404","7401 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd ibn Anas, he said: I entered with my grandfather Anas ibn Malik to al-Hakam ibn Ayyub, and there were people who had set up a chicken as a target shooting at it. Anas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that animals be tied up (as targets). And this wording we do not know anyone narrated except Anas."
"7405","7402 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: A woman from the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was alone with her, and he said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you are the most beloved of people to me."
"7406","7403 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Umm Sulaym."
"7407","7404 - He said: And Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Hisham ibn Zayd, from Anas; that Umm Sulaym said: O Messenger of Allah, Anas ibn Malik - I think she said, your little servant - supplicate to Allah for him. He said: O Allah, increase his wealth and children, and bless for him in what You have given him."
"7408","7405 - Ahmad ibn Abi Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Miskin ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go around his wives with a single washing."
"7409","7406 - And Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hanan narrated it to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Shu'bah except Miskin ibn Bukayr and Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid."
"7410","7407 - Salih ibn Adi ibn Abi Imarah al-Dharra' narrated to us, al-Sumayda' ibn Wahib narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to like pumpkin. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Shu'bah except al-Sumayda'."
"7411","7408 - al-Husayn ibn Abi Kabshah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the Hour comes while in the hand of one of you is a seedling, let him plant it. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Hisham ibn Zayd except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"7412","Tawbah al-Anbari, from Anas. 7409 - Abdah ibn Abdillah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, Muti' ibn Rashid narrated to us, Tawbah al-Anbari narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank milk and did not rinse his mouth."
"7413","7410 - Abdah ibn Abdillah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, Muti' ibn Rashid narrated to us, Tawbah al-Anbari narrated to me: that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Look who is in the mosque and call him. So I entered, meaning the mosque, and there were Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, so I called them. I brought him something and placed it before him; he ate and they ate, then they went out and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in the morning prayer. And we do not know Tawbah al-Anbari narrated from Anas except these two hadiths, and none narrated them from him except Muti' ibn Rashid."
"7414","Mu'adh ibn Harmalah, from Anas. 7411 - Abdah ibn Abdillah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Harmalah narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come upon people a time when the sky rains a general rain, but the earth will not grow anything."
"7415","Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas. 7412 - Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jud'an said, Anas ibn Malik said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gesturing with his hand: I took hold of the ring of the gate of Paradise and rattled it."
"7416","7413 - And Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, he said: Ibn Jud'an said, meaning Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud'an, from Anas, he said: Abu Talhah used to kneel before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in battle, then say: My face as ransom for your face, and my soul as protection for your soul. He said, and he said, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The voice of Abu Talhah in the army is better than a group."
"7417","7414 - Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jud'an, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: Some seventy killed of the Ansar - meaning the day of Uhud, and the day of Bi'r Ma'unah, and two other days, one of them the day of Yamamah."
"7418","7415 - Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw in what a sleeper sees as though the tip of my sword broke, and as though I had a ram behind me. I interpreted that the tip of my sword was the killing of a man of my people, and that my having a ram behind me meant I would kill the ram (chief) of the people. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) killed Talhah ibn Abi Talhah - and he was the flag-bearer of the polytheists - and Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib was killed. And this hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain, and none narrated it from Ali except Hammad."
"7419","7416 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first to be clothed - I think he said, on the Day of Resurrection - with a garment of Fire is Iblis; he places it on his eyebrows and drags it behind him - I think he said - and his offspring follow behind him, until he stands over the Fire and calls out: O my destruction, and they call out: O our destruction. It will be said to them: Do not call today for one destruction but call for many destructions. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated except Anas, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Ali ibn Zayd except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"7420","7417 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us. 7418 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, meaning Ibn Salamah, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I passed on the night I was taken by night (Isra) over people whose lips were being cut with scissors of fire. I said: O Jibril, who are these? He said: These are the preachers of your ummah who command people to righteousness and forget themselves. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Ali ibn Zayd other than Hammad ibn Salamah among those whose hadith is used as proof."
"7421","7419 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pass by the house of Fatimah when he went out for the Fajr prayer and say: O people of the House, the prayer: Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O people of the House, and to purify you thoroughly."
"7422","7420 - Umar ibn Musa al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd and Qatadah and Humayd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I hear the crying of a child behind me while I am in prayer, so I shorten it - I think he said - because of what I know of his mother's distress."
"7423","7421 - Rawh ibn Hatim and Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Adami narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Musa was a shy man, and he came - I think he said - to water to bathe, and placed his clothes on a rock. His private parts were hardly ever visible. The Children of Israel said: Musa is afflicted with a hernia and has a defect, meaning he does not put down his clothes. The rock carried away his clothes until it came alongside the gatherings of the Children of Israel, and they looked at Musa (peace be upon him) as the finest of men, or as he said. That is His saying: So Allah declared him innocent of what they said, and he was honorable before Allah. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Anas except with this chain, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Hammad except Yahya ibn Hammad and Ubaydullah ibn A'ishah."
"7424","7422 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas: that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was hard pressed, he said: Who will repel them from us, and he will be my companion in Paradise? A man from the Ansar stood and fought until he was killed, then another stood and fought until seven were killed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have not done justice to our companions."
"7425","7423 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad was brought the head of al-Husayn ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with them, and it was placed before him. He began tapping with a stick in his hand on his teeth and saying: He had beautiful front teeth indeed, and saying: By Allah, I will surely grieve you. I said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissing the place of your stick on his mouth. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, except Sulayman ibn Harb, and others narrated it from Thabit."
"7426","7424 - al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, he said: The king of Rome gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a mustaqah (long garment), either of sundus or of silk. Some of his companions touched it, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The handkerchiefs of Sa'd in Paradise are better than it."
"7427","7425 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knew that the mountain path is better than the valley."
"7428","7426 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Anas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed the spoils of Hunayn, the Ansar felt something in themselves and said: He distributes booty among them while our swords drip with their blood. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he sat in a tent of hair and sent for the Ansar, and they came. He said: O company of the Ansar, is there among you anyone from other than you? They said: No, except a sister's son of ours. He said: The sister's son of a people is of them. Then he said: O company of the Ansar, did I not come to you astray and Allah guided you through me? They said: Yes. Or he said: Did I not find you astray and Allah guided you through me? Did I not come to you humiliated and Allah aided you through me? They said: Yes. He said: Then he fell silent a while, then said: If you wished you could say: You came to us denied and we believed you, you came to us expelled and we sheltered you, you came to us forsaken and we aided you. Are you not pleased that the people go with sheep - I think he said - and camels, and you return with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to your houses? They said: Yes. He said: If the people take a valley and you take a mountain path, I would take your mountain path; and were it not for the Hijrah, I would be a man of the Ansar. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Ali ibn Zayd in its entirety except Abd al-Warith."
"7429","7427 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, he said: We were rained upon with hail in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Talhah would eat of it while fasting. I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Take from your uncle. And in this hadith Ali ibn Zayd differed from Qatadah in his narration."
"7430","7428 - Hilal ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: I saw Abu Talhah eating hail while fasting, and saying: It is neither food nor drink. He said: I mentioned that to Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, and he disliked it and said: It cuts thirst. And we do not know this act was narrated except from Abu Talhah."
"7431","7429 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas as far as I know: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is not one who spends the night full while his neighbor is hungry. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated with this chain except Husayn ibn Ali, and we do not know it to be narrated from Anas from any route except this one."
"7432","7430 (m) - al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah al-Bazzar narrated to us, Abu al-Nadr Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Ammi narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The habitual drinker of wine will not enter the gardens of Firdaws, nor the disobedient to parents, nor the one who reminds of his giving. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Ali ibn Zayd except Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Ammi."
"7433","7431 - al-Walid ibn Sufyan al-Attar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: A slave girl would take the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and go with him wherever she wished; he would not refuse her. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Ali ibn Zayd except Shu'bah."
"7434","7432 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abu Nasr al-Tammar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd and Yunus and Humayd, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is one whom people trust; the Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand Muslims are safe; the emigrant is one who abandons evil; and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, no servant will enter Paradise whose neighbor is not safe from his harms."
"7435","7433 - Khalifah ibn Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Salim Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, how will people be gathered on their faces? He said: The One Who made them walk on their feet is able to make them walk on their faces."
"7436","7434 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, he said: The muezzin would call the adhan in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and one would think it was the iqamah because of how many would stand and pray the two rak'ahs before Maghrib."
"7437","7435 - And al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated it to us, Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, Abu Safwan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Thabit, from Anas, with something similar."
"7438","7436 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, from Abu Dawud, from Talhah ibn Amr, from Thabit, from Anas, with something similar to the hadith of Ali ibn Zayd. And we do not know Ata narrated from Thabit, from Anas, except this hadith; none narrated it from Ibn Jurayj except Abu Safwan, and he was a man who settled in Makkah, there is no harm in him. This narration we do not know anyone narrated except Anas, and it has been narrated from Anas through various routes; it is contradicted by the hadith of Buraydah that he said: Between every two adhans is a prayer except Maghrib."
"7439","7437 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, he said: A servant girl of the people of Madinah would take the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would not withdraw his hand from her until she took him wherever she wished."
"7440","Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab, from Anas. 7438 - Ubaydullah ibn al-Jahm al-Anmati narrated to us, Damrah ibn Rabi'ah narrated to us, from Sufyan, meaning al-Thawri, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah and made her freedom her dowry."
"7441","7439 - And Abu Kamil narrated it to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, and from Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"7442","7440 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, Hammad ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, from Hisham, meaning Ibn Abi Abdillah, from Shu'ayb, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the same. And we do not know Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated from Shu'ayb, from Anas, other than this hadith; none narrated it from Yunus except al-Thawri, and a group narrated it from al-Thawri. And we do not know Hisham narrated from Shu'ayb other than this hadith, and it is well known from Shu'ayb."
"7443","7441 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Shu'ayb narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Safiyyah and made her freedom her dowry, and held a wedding feast for her with hays (a dish of dates, ghee and cheese)."
"7444","7442 - Amr ibn Yahya ibn Ghufrah al-Bajali narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have urged you much regarding the siwak."
"7445","7443 - Amr ibn Yahya ibn Ghufrah al-Bajali narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'ayb, from Anas; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal is one-eyed; written between his eyes is 'disbeliever'; every reader and non-reader will read it."
"7446","7444 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, meaning Ibn Salamah, from Humayd and Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"7447","7445 - Muhammad al-Muthanna narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Ta'i narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most complete of people in faith are the best of them in character; and good character indeed reaches the rank of fasting and prayer. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Shu'ayb, from Anas, except Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn al-Subayh al-Ta'i."
"7448","7446 - And Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam al-Qaysi narrated it to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab narrated to us, from his father, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The congregational prayer exceeds the prayer of a man alone by twenty-five prayers."
"7449","7447 - Ahmad ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Nu'aym narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dream of the believer is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Shu'ayb except Sa'id ibn Zayd, nor from Sa'id except Muhammad ibn Abi Nu'aym."
"7450","7448 - al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Ataki narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Shu'ayb ibn al-Hijab narrated to us, from his father, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Azd are the Azd of Allah on His earth; people want to lower them, but Allah refuses except to raise them. The world will not end until a man wishes and says: Would that my father were Azdi, would that my mother were Azdi."
"7451","al-Ja'd Abu Uthman, from Anas. 7449 - Talut ibn Abbad narrated to us, Bakr ibn Khunays narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from al-Ja'd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never led us in an obligatory prayer except that when he turned to us with his face he said: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from every deed that disgraces, and I seek refuge in You from every companion that destroys, and I seek refuge in You from every hope that distracts, and I seek refuge in You from every poverty - or from a poverty that makes forget - and I seek refuge in You from every richness that makes transgress. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Anas except al-Ja'd, nor anyone narrated it from al-Ja'd except Abu Imran al-Jawni. Abu Imran narrated from al-Ja'd only this hadith, and none narrated it from Abu Imran except Bakr ibn Khunays, and he is not strong; and we do not know anyone else narrated it."
"7452","7450 - Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Idris narrated to us, Ja'far, meaning Ibn Sulayman, narrated to us, al-Ja'd narrated to us, from Anas, he said: My mother said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you, Anas - if you would supplicate for him with some supplications. So he supplicated for me with three supplications: two in this world, and I have seen them, and I hope for the third in the Hereafter."
"7453","Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Anas, from Anas. 7451 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Anas narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: that a man peeped from one of the rooms of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a barbed arrowhead, or barbed arrowheads - Anas said: It is as if I am looking at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He went - I think he said - and threw it at him, or stabbed him, but missed him - Hammad doubted."
"7454","7452 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Anas; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has entrusted an angel with the womb, and he says: O Lord, a drop; O Lord, a clot; O Lord, a lump. When Allah, Blessed and Exalted, intends to create it, he says: O Lord, male or female, wretched or happy; what is the provision and what is the lifespan? He said: So that is written in its mother's belly. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Anas except with this chain."
"7455","7453 - Yahya ibn Habib ibn Adi narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7456","7454 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Yahya ibn Kathir narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the major sins: associating partners with Allah, Blessed and Exalted, disobedience to parents, killing a soul, and false speech. And we do not know anything narrated from Anas regarding the major sins except from the hadith of Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Anas."
"7457","7455 - Abdah ibn Abdillah narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fudalah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Anas, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: Bring out of the Fire - I think he said - whoever remembered Me for a day, or feared Me in a station."
"7458","7456 - Muhammad ibn Sudran narrated to us, Anbasah ibn Salim, the keeper of the tablets, narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Anas, from Anas; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a man put on sandals while standing. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Anas except from this route, and none narrated it from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr except Anbasah. Anbasah narrated hadiths from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Anas, and we do not know him to have been corroborated in this hadith."
"7459","7457 - Suhayl ibn Ibrahim al-Jarudi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salam, the keeper of the Tayalisah, narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not go out on the day of Fitr until he ate some dates before going out."
"7460","7458 - Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Help your brother, oppressor or oppressed. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, this one we help as oppressed, but how about him as oppressor? He said: You prevent him, or turn him back from his oppression, or a word like it."
"7461","7459 - Ali ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, from Anas; that some people of Uraynah, or Ukl, came to Madinah and found it unhealthy. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent them out with his camels, or with the charity camels. When they recovered, they killed the herdsman and drove off the camels. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent after them; they were brought, and he cut off their hands and feet and gouged their eyes."
"7462","7460 - And Harun ibn Sufyan and al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated it to us, they said: Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only gouged the eyes of the Uraniyyun because they had gouged the eyes of the herdsmen."
"7463","7461 - Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, Yahya ibn Kathir narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dog, the donkey and the woman cut off the prayer."
"7464","And from the hadith of Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah also from Anas. 7462 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Husayn ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Simak, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas."
"7465","7463 - And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated it to us, Abu Ghassan narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Some people of Uraynah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), embraced Islam and pledged allegiance to him, while an epidemic had fallen in Madinah - I think he said, an epidemic. They said: The epidemic has fallen in Madinah; if you permit us we would go out to the camels and stay among them. So they went out, killed the herdsman, took the camels; and with him (the Prophet) were youths of the Ansar, nearly twenty. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent them and sent with them a tracker to follow their tracks. They were brought, and he cut off their hands and feet and branded their eyes. And this hadith has been narrated from Anas through various routes with different wordings, and we do not know in any other hadith of those who narrated it from Anas that he sent a tracker with them except in this hadith. Simak narrated from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas, only this hadith."
"7466","Ali ibn Zayd also from Anas. 7464 - al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, he said: You do deeds that are finer in your eyes than hair; we used to count them in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as destructive sins. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Ali ibn Zayd except Sa'id ibn Zayd."
"7467","7465 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, he said: The oldest of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, and Suhayl ibn Amr."
"7468","7466 - al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fudalah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The children of the polytheists are servants of the people of Paradise."
"7469","7467 - And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Wasiti narrated it to us, Mu'alla ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fudalah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, with something similar, but he did not raise it (to the Prophet)."
"7470","7468 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Sharik, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited the talbiyah for both (Hajj and Umrah together)."
"7471","Amr ibn Sa'id, from Anas. 7469 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ashhal ibn Hatim narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Amr ibn Sa'id, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would visit his wives. He came to a woman he had newly married, and there were people with them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went off, remained away and relieved himself, then came back after they had gone. He said: He entered and let down a curtain between me and him. He said: I went to Abu Talhah - I think he said - and informed him. He said: If it is as you say, something will be revealed about this. Then the verse of hijab was revealed. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Ibn Awn except Ashhal. Ashhal was narrated from by Ibn Wahb, and he is well known of the people of Basra."
"7472","Ziyad ibn Abi Hassan, from Anas. 7470 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Abi Hassan, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever aids one in distress, Allah writes for him seventy-three pardons; one of them contains rectification of all his affairs, and seventy-two until the Day of Resurrection, or He stores them for him on the Day of Resurrection. And we do not know Ziyad ibn Abi Hassan narrated from Anas except this hadith."
"7473","Ali ibn Zayd also from Anas. 7471 - Bishr ibn Khalid and Ahmad ibn Sinan narrated to us, they said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Husayn informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas; that the king of Dhi Yazan gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a jar of manna, and he accepted it."
"7474","Wahb ibn Manus, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Anas. 7472 - Salamah ibn Shabib and Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, they said: Abdullah ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn Kaysan narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Wahb ibn Manus, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Anas, he said: I have not seen anyone whose prayer resembled the Messenger of Allah's more than this boy, meaning Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz; we estimated ten glorifications in his bowing and ten glorifications in his prostration. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Anas except from this route, nor do we know this wording from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this route with this chain. Wahb ibn Manus - we do not know anyone narrated from him except Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn Kaysan, a man of the people of Sana'a."
"7475","al-Sha'bi. 7473 - Ali ibn al-Fadl al-Karabisi narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Thaqafi, from Amir, meaning al-Sha'bi, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by and saw a tent. He said: O Anas, whose tent is this? I said: So-and-so's. He said: Every building is a calamity upon its owner on the Day of Resurrection, unless he builds a house to inhabit. That reached the Ansari, so he demolished it. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from al-Sha'bi, from Anas, except from this route with this chain."
"7476","7474 - And Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated it to us, my father narrated to us, from Utbah Abu Amr, from al-Sha'bi, from Anas, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and he said: Who will guard us tonight? I said: I will. He slept, the people slept, and I slept. We did not wake except by the heat of the sun. He said: O people, these souls are a trust in the bodies of servants; He takes them and sends them when He wills. Attend to your needs calmly. So we attended to our needs calmly, performed ablution, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, prayed the two rak'ahs of Fajr before the prayer, then led us in prayer. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from al-Sha'bi, from Anas, except Utbah; none narrated it except Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi."
"7477","7475 - Hamdan ibn Ali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Abbas ibn Dhurayh, from al-Sha'bi, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted ruqyah for every poisonous sting. Al-Abbas ibn Dhurayh was contradicted in this hadith: Mujalid said, from al-Sha'bi, from Jabir; Husayn said, from al-Sha'bi, from Imran ibn Husayn - some raised it (to the Prophet), some did not raise it; and some said, from Husayn, from al-Sha'bi, from Buraydah."
"7478","7476 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Ali ibn Qadim narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ubayd al-Mukattib, from al-Sha'bi, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed one day, or smiled, and said: Will you not ask me about what I laughed? They said: O Messenger of Allah, what did you laugh about? He said: I marveled at the servant's disputing with his Lord on the Day of Resurrection; he says: O Lord, did You not promise me that You would not wrong me? He says: Yes. He says: I accept no witness against me except from myself. He says: Then the Blessed and Exalted says: Is it not enough that I am a witness, and the noble recording angels as witnesses? He says: He repeats this speech several times. He says: Then his mouth is sealed, and his limbs speak of what he used to do. He says: Away with you and perdition; it was for you I was disputing: And you did not conceal yourselves lest your hearing and your sights bear witness against you."
"7479","And al-Thawri narrated it, from Ubayd al-Mukattib, from Fudayl ibn Amr, from al-Sha'bi, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 7477 - Ibn Ibrahim ibn Abdillah ibn Muhammad Abu Shaybah narrated it to us, Minjab narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Asadi narrated to us, from al-Thawri, from Ubayd al-Mukattib, from Fudayl ibn Amr, from al-Sha'bi, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And we do not know al-Sha'bi narrated from Anas except these hadiths."
"7480","Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, from Anas. 7478 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Bahrani narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Sallam, from Hammad, meaning Ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ibrahim, meaning al-Nakha'i, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim."
"7481","7479 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated it to us, Hafs ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Shinzhir, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And we do not know al-Nakha'i narrated from Anas except this hadith. Ibrahim ibn Sallam - we do not know anyone narrated from him except Abu Asim. This hadith has been narrated from Anas through various routes and chains; all that is narrated in that from Anas is not strong; and what we mentioned is of the best of them in chain."
"7482","7480 - al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Rukhami narrated to us, Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn Adi, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a woman prays her five, fasts her month, guards her chastity, and obeys her husband, she enters Paradise."
"7483","7481 - al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub and Humayd ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, they said: Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn Adi, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever avoids four enters Paradise: blood, wealth, private parts, and drinks. These two hadiths we do not know anyone narrated except Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording, except al-Zubayr ibn Adi; we do not know anyone narrated them from al-Zubayr except al-Thawri, nor from al-Thawri except Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah. Rawwad is sound in hadith but not strong; a group of scholars narrated from him and accepted his hadith."
"7484","7482 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Uthman ibn Za'idah narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn Adi, from Anas, he said: No time comes upon you except that which follows it is worse than it, until you meet your Lord. I heard that from your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or as he said. He said: If it is so, if Allah wills. And this hadith a group narrated from al-Zubayr ibn Adi, from Anas; we do not know anyone narrated it from Mis'ar except Uthman ibn Za'idah, so we sufficed with the hadith of Mis'ar from al-Zubayr."
"7485","7483 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la ibn Amir al-Taghlibi, from Bilal ibn Mirdas, from Khaythamah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever seeks judgeship and asks intercessors for it is left to himself; whoever is compelled to it, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sends down upon him an angel to guide him. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from Anas from this route, nor from other than Anas preserved from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording. Isra'il narrated this hadith from Abd al-A'la, from Bilal ibn Mirdas, from Anas, without mentioning Khaythamah."
"7486","7484 - Sa'id ibn Bahr al-Qaratisî narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr narrated to us, Salih ibn Umar narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashja'i, from Anas, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. He said: If there comes from her what comes from a man, let her wash. And we do not know Abu Malik narrated from Anas except this hadith; none narrated it from him except Salih ibn Umar, and he is Wasiti."
"7487","7485 - al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us. 7486 - And Bishr ibn Khalid narrated it to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is indeed pleased with the servant that he eats a meal or drinks a drink and praises Allah for it."
"7488","7487 - al-Hasan ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah, from Anas, he said: I served the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) nine years, and he never once said to me: Why did you not do such-and-such, nor said: Why did you do - or - not do such-and-such. And we do not know Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah narrated from Anas except these two hadiths; we do not know anyone narrated them from him except Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah; and Abu Malik narrated from Anas only that hadith."
"7489","7488 - al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the first intercessor in Paradise, and I am the prophets' most followed on the Day of Resurrection. Among the prophets will be one who comes on the Day of Resurrection with none but one with him, meaning one man."
"7490","7489 - Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas, he said: It was said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), O best of creation. He said: That is my father Ibrahim."
"7491","7490 - And Salamah ibn Shabib narrated it to us, al-Firyabi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas, he said: A man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), O best of creation. He said: That is my father Ibrahim. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Anas, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Anas except al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful."
"7492","7491 - Humayd ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the first to knock on the gate of Paradise. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from al-Thawri except Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham."
"7493","7492 - al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani narrated to me, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one day - I think he said, when he finished - he said: O people, I am your imam, so do not precede me in bowing nor in prostration, and do not raise your heads - I think he said, before me - for I see you from in front of me and from behind me. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if you saw what I saw you would laugh little and weep much. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what did you see? He said: I saw Paradise and Hell."
"7494","7493 - al-Sari ibn Asim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I asked him about drinking in vessels, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade pitched vessels, and said: Every intoxicant is unlawful."
"7495","7494 - al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Malik narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas, he said: Leave what makes you doubt for what does not make you doubt, for it is a wise saying those before you held to. And he said: Every intoxicant is unlawful, and whatever intoxicates in large amount, its small amount is unlawful."
"7496","7495 - Muhammad ibn Salih al-Adawi narrated it to us, al-Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from Humayd and al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and saw in it a palace of gold. I said: Whose palace is this? It was said: For a man of Quraysh. I asked, or it was said to me, Umar ibn al-Khattab - I think he said - were it not for your jealousy I would have entered it. Umar said: Would I be jealous regarding you, O Messenger of Allah? And this hadith is well known from Humayd, from Anas; as for from al-Mukhtar, we do not know anyone narrated it except Husayn ibn Ali, from Za'idah."
"7497","7496 - Ibn Abi al-Bakhtari narrated to us, and I think his name is Muhammad, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dozed in the mosque and woke up smiling. They said: What are you laughing about? He said: A surah was revealed to me while I dozed: Indeed We have given you al-Kawthar. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is al-Kawthar? He said: A river in which is a basin, in which are cups as many as the stars of the sky; my ummah will come to it, and a man among them will be snatched away. I will say: O Lord, my ummah. It will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you. Or I say: O Lord, from my ummah. It will be said: You do not know what he innovated after you."
"7498","7497 - And Safwan ibn Mughallis narrated it to us, Bakr ibn Khidash narrated to us, al-Thawri narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"7499","7498 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sulayman al-Dabbas narrated to us, Bakr ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the garden of a man, and a man came and sought entrance. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Anas, stand and open for him and give him tidings of Paradise, and that he will assume the affairs of my ummah after me. And there was Abu Bakr. This hadith is only known from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas, from the hadith of Bakr ibn al-Mukhtar, and he was not corroborated in it."
"7500","7499 - Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: People will keep asking - or people will never cease asking - about everything until they say: This is Allah Who created everything, so who created Him?"
"7501","7500 - And Ali ibn Sahl al-Mada'ini narrated it to us, al-Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from worry and grief, incapacity and laziness, miserliness and cowardice, the burden of debt and the domination of men."
"7502","7501 - Amr ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abu Amr Utbah narrated to us, from Abu Rawq, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the garden of a man of the Ansar, and a man came and sought entrance. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Anas, stand and open for him, give him tidings of Paradise, and inform him that he will lead my ummah after me. So I stood and opened for him, and there was Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him. I gave him tidings, he praised Allah, then entered. Then another came and knocked on the door. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Stand, O Anas, open for him, give him tidings of Paradise, and inform him that he will assume the affairs of my ummah after Abu Bakr. I opened for him, and there was Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. I gave him tidings, he praised Allah, then entered. Then another came and knocked on the door. He said: O Anas, stand and open for him, give him tidings of Paradise - and I think he said - and inform him that he will assume the affairs of my ummah after Abu Bakr and Umar, and that he will meet harshness from the subjects, so command him at that time to restrain himself. I opened for him, and there was Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with them. I gave him tidings, he praised Allah, and I informed him of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Anas except from two routes, this being one of them."
"7503","7502 - And the other route: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, from Ibrahim ibn Sulayman, Bakr ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, he said: I met him in Kufa, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas. And in both routes, they are not strong. And we do not know Abu Rawq narrated from Anas except this hadith."
"7504","7503 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas, he said: Jibril came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day while he was sad, sitting, struck by some of the people of Makkah; they had stained him with blood. He said: What is wrong with you? He said: These people did this to me. He said: Would you like me to show you a sign? He said: Yes. He said: He looked at a tree beyond the valley and said: Call this tree. He called it, and it came walking until it stood before him. Then he said to it: Return, and it returned until it went back to its place. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It suffices me. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Anas except from this route."
"7505","7504 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out angry and said: Do not ask me today about anything except that I will tell you of it. And we thought Jibril (peace be upon him) was with him. A man stood to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, who is my father? He said: Your father is so-and-so, the father he was attributed to. They asked him about things. Then Umar stood to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, we were recently in ignorance; do not expose our faults against us, nor disgrace us by our secrets; pardon us, may Allah pardon you. We are pleased with Allah as Lord, Islam as religion, and Muhammad as messenger. He said: I have never seen the like of today in good and evil; Paradise and Hell were shown to me below the wall. I never saw a day with more weepers than that day. This hadith has been narrated from Anas through various routes, and in this hadith is speech not in the hadith of others."
"7506","7505 - al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim al-Anbari and Ibrahim ibn Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Kufi narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah narrated to us, from his father, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us one day angry, and we thought Jibril (peace be upon him) was with him, until he ascended the pulpit. I never saw a day with more weepers covering their faces than it. He said: Ask me; by Allah, you will not ask me about anything except that I will inform you of it. A man stood to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, who is my father? He said: Your father is Hudhafah, the one he was attributed to. Another stood to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, am I in Paradise or in Hell? He said: No, rather in Hell. Another stood to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, is Hajj upon us every year? He said: If I said it, it would become obligatory; if it became obligatory you would not fulfill it; if you did not fulfill it you would be punished. He said: Umar ibn al-Khattab stood up, may Allah's mercy be upon him, and said: We are pleased with Allah as Lord, Islam as religion, and Muhammad as messenger. We were recently in ignorance, so do not expose our faults, nor disgrace us by our secrets; pardon us, may Allah pardon you. He said: His distress was relieved. Then he turned toward the wall and said: I never saw the like of today in good and evil; Paradise and Hell were brought near to this wall. And this hadith with these wordings we do not know anyone narrated except Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah, from his father, from al-A'mash; we do not know it narrated from Anas that a man said, O Messenger of Allah, is Hajj every year, except from this route."
"7507","7506 - Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah narrated to us, from his father, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas."
"7508","7507 - And Ibrahim ibn Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Kufi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from his father, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas - and the wording is that of Ibrahim ibn Abdillah - he said: They beat the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day until he fainted. Abu Bakr stood and said: Woe to you, would you kill a man for saying, My Lord is Allah? They said: Who is this? They said: This is Ibn Abi Quhafah, the madman - I think he said - so they left him and turned upon Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with them. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Anas except from this route; we do not know anyone narrated it from al-A'mash except Abu Ubaydah, and none narrated from Abu Ubaydah except his son Muhammad."
"7509","7508 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would often say: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. We said: O Messenger of Allah, we believed in you and what you brought; do you fear for us? He said: Yes; hearts are between two fingers of the fingers of Allah; He turns them. And this hadith others than Abu Mu'awiyah narrated from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir."
"7510","7509 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the believer is like a feather in a desert, the wind turns it over once and sets it upright another time. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from al-A'mash with this chain except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash. Others differed with him: others than Abu Bakr narrated it from al-A'mash, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Ghunaym ibn Qays, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7511","7510 - Ibrahim ibn Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Kufi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sharik narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man of fine appearance came; they mentioned good things of his affair. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I see on his face a mark of the Fire. When he came and greeted, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah you came - he mentioned a word - I think he said: Did you say in yourself - or - do you see in yourself that you are the best of the people? He said: Yes. He said: When he went, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There has risen among my ummah - I think he said - a people, this one and his companions among them. Abu Bakr said: Shall I not kill him, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes. Abu Bakr went and found him praying in the mosque, and returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I found him praying and could not kill him. Umar said: Shall I not kill him? He said: Yes. He said: Umar went and found him in the mosque praying, bowing. He returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I found him praying and could not kill him. Ali said: Shall I not kill him, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes, you kill him if you find him. Ali went and did not find him. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Anas with this wording except from this route; we do not know anyone narrated it from al-A'mash except Sharik."
"7512","7511 - Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us, Ali ibn Yazid al-Hanafi narrated to us, Sa'd ibn al-Salt narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas, he said: Twenty youths of the Ansar would attend the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for his needs; when he intended a matter he sent them in it."
"7513","7512 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Sa'd ibn al-Salt narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, and with it from Anas - and I did not find in my book from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and I think it is raised - he said: Whoever goes out in the path of Allah comes on the Day of Resurrection with his blood at its fullest flow; its color saffron, its scent the scent of musk, upon him the seal of the martyrs. These two hadiths we do not know to be narrated from Anas except from this route; we do not know anyone narrated them from al-A'mash except Sa'd ibn al-Salt. Abu Sufyan's name is Talhah ibn Nafi'; al-A'mash narrated much hadith from him, and his hearing from him has been questioned."
"7514","7513 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, Shabib ibn Bishr al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two voices are cursed in this world and the Hereafter: a flute at a blessing, and wailing at a calamity. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Anas except with this chain."
"7515","7514 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, Shabib ibn Bishr narrated to us, Anas narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has not bestowed a blessing upon a servant and he says, Alhamdulillah, except that what he gave is better than what he took. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Anas except from this route with this chain."
"7516","7515 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, Shabib narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever shoots an arrow in the path of Allah, whether it falls short or reaches, will have the reward like that of freeing four persons of the children of Isma'il."
"7517","7516 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Shabib ibn Bishr, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed regarding wine ten: its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its buyer, its seller, the carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its drinker, its server, and the eater of its price. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Anas except from this route."
"7518","7517 - And with it he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever goes for an evening march - meaning in the path of Allah - will have - I think he said - what dust touches him as musk on the Day of Resurrection."
"7519","7518 - And with it he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the signs of the Hour are obscenity, foul speech, severing kinship, trusting the treacherous - I think he said - and distrusting the trustworthy, or a word like it."
"7520","7519 - Zayd ibn Akhzam Abu Talib al-Ta'i narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Shabib ibn Bishr, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to A'ishah: Hand me the prayer mat. She said: I am menstruating. He said: Your menstruation is not in your hand. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Anas except from this route with this chain."
"7521","7520 - Nasr ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Washsha' al-Kufi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Bashir narrated to us, Shabib ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The guide to good is like its doer."
"7522","7521 - And Bishr ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, al-Sakan ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Ziyad al-Numayri, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The guide to good is like its doer, and Allah loves aiding the distressed."
"7523","7522 - al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, Zafir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Shabib, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All spending is in the path of Allah except this building; there is no good in it. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from other than Anas with this wording from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7524","7523 - Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Kabir al-Attar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Khuza'i narrated to us, from Anbasah, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Shabib, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless my ummah in its early morning on its Thursday. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Anas except from this route; Anbasah ibn Abd al-Rahman is lenient in hadith."
"7525","7524 - Nasr ibn Ali and Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, and the wording is Nasr's, Jarir, meaning Ibn Abd al-Hamid, informed us; and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Mu'ammal narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us. 7525 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Rib'i, from Abu al-Abyad, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would lead us in Asr while the sun was white, high - Mu'ammal added in his hadith from al-Thawri: Anas said - so I go to my family and say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has prayed, so stand and pray. And we do not know Abu al-Abyad narrated any hadith other than this; we do not know anyone narrated from him except Rib'i ibn Hirash."
"7526","7526 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My basin is from such-and-such to such-and-such; in it are vessels as many as the stars, sweeter in scent than musk, sweeter than honey, colder than snow, whiter than milk. Whoever drinks a drink from it will never thirst again; whoever does not drink from it will never be quenched. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated with this wording except from Anas with this chain; we do not know Adi ibn Thabit narrated from Anas except this hadith, and none narrated it from him except al-Mas'udi."
"7527","Uthman ibn Umayr. 7527 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Umar ibn Yunus al-Yamami narrated to us, Jahdam ibn Abdillah narrated to us, Abu Taybah narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Umayr, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril (peace be upon him) came to me with a white mirror in his hand in which was a black spot. I said: What is this, O Jibril? He said: This is Friday; your Lord obliges it upon you, to be a festival for you - or - for your people after you; you are the first, and the Jews and Christians are after you. He said: What is in it for us? He said: In it is good for you; in it is an hour in which whoever supplicates his Lord for good allotted to him, He gives it to him - or not allotted to him, yet stored for him what is greater than it - or seeks refuge in it from evil decreed upon him, He protects him from what is greater than it. He said: I said: What is this black spot in it? He said: It is the Hour occurring on Friday; it is the chief of days with us, and we call it in the Hereafter the Day of Increase. He said: I said: Why do you call it the Day of Increase? He said: Your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, has taken in Paradise a wide valley of white musk. When Friday comes, the Blessed and Exalted descends from Illiyyun upon His Kursi; then the Kursi is surrounded with pulpits of light, and the prophets come until they sit upon them; then the pulpits are surrounded with chairs of gold, then the truthful and the martyrs come until they sit upon them; then the people of Paradise come until they sit upon the sandhill. Their Lord, Blessed and Exalted, manifests Himself to them until they look at His Face, and He says: I am the One Who fulfilled My promise to you, completed My favor upon you; this is the place of My honor, so ask Me. They ask Him for contentment; the Mighty and Majestic says: My contentment settles you in My abode and grants you My honor, so ask Me. They ask Him until their desires end. Thereupon is opened for them what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, nor occurred to a human heart, until the time people disperse from Friday. Then the Blessed and Exalted ascends upon His Kursi; the martyrs and the truthful ascend with Him - I think he said - and the people of the chambers return to their chambers: a white pearl with no crack in it nor flaw, or a red ruby, or a green chrysolite; from them are their chambers, their doors set in rows, their rivers flowing within, their fruits hanging low, their spouses and servants within. They need nothing as much as Friday, to be increased in honor therein and to increase in looking at His Face, Blessed and Exalted; therefore it is called the Day of Increase. And this hadith a group narrated, among them Ibrahim ibn Tahman, Muhammad ibn Fudayl and others, from Layth, from Uthman ibn Umayr, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7528","7528 - I heard Abdullah ibn al-Waddah al-Kufi narrating from Yahya ibn Yaman, from Sharik, from Uthman ibn Umayr, from Anas, regarding the saying of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: And with Us is more: he said, He manifests Himself to them every Friday. And Uthman is righteous. This hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Anas with this wording except Uthman ibn Umayr Abu al-Yaqzan."
"7529","A'idh ibn Shurayh. 7529 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Humayd ibn Hammad ibn Abi al-Khuwar narrated to us, A'idh ibn Shurayh narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of the Ansar, give gifts to one another, for gifts remove malice. If a trotter were gifted to me I would accept it, and if I were invited to an arm I would answer."
"7530","7530 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Humayd ibn Hammad narrated to us, A'idh ibn Shurayh narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting and looked at a hole and said: If hardship came until it entered this hole, ease would come until it expelled it. Then he said: Indeed with hardship is ease. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Anas except A'idh ibn Shurayh."
"7531","7531 - Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Ubaydah al-Usfuri narrated to us, Bakr ibn Bakkar narrated to us, A'idh ibn Shurayh narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies about me in narrating a hadith, let him take his seat in the Fire. It has been narrated from Anas through various routes that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies about me deliberately. We do not know anyone who said, in narrating a hadith, except A'idh ibn Shurayh."
"7532","Matar ibn Maymun. 7532 - I found in my book in my handwriting, from Abu Kurayb, from Yunus ibn Bukayr, from Matar ibn Maymun, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: I was serving the people figs and raisins mixed together. Among the people was a man called Abu Bakr, a man of Kinanah. When he drank he said - while we were thus and the people were drinking, a Muslim man entered upon us and said: What are you doing? Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has sent down the prohibition of wine. So we spilled the vat and overturned it. Then we went out and found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing on the pulpit reciting this verse repeatedly: Satan only intends to cause enmity and hatred among you through wine and gambling, and to turn you away from the remembrance of Allah and from prayer; so will you desist? And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Anas with this wording except from this route. Matar ibn Maymun al-Kufi narrated from Anas hadiths, and from others."
"7533","Abu Sa'd al-Baqqal Sa'id ibn al-Marzuban. 7533 - Ishaq ibn Ziyad al-Ayli and Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Hayyaj narrated to us, they said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Sa'd narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The father of Anas died, and a man of the Ansar called Abu Talhah married his mother after him. It was not long before she bore him a boy. He remained until he grew; the boy desired something, and his father went out and did not return until his son died. She covered him and closed his eyes. Abu Talhah came and said: How is my son? She said: He is calmer than ever, and today he is better for you. He said: And he lay with her, and they poured water over themselves. Then she said: What do you say of people who borrowed a loan from people, and when they sought it back they were displeased? He said: Evil is what they did. She said: The borrowed one is your son; he has died. Allah has given you his reward. He said: He uttered istirja', then went out to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him and how she spoke. He said: O Allah, bless them in their night together. He said: It was not long before she bore him a boy, and he named him Abdullah. He did not die until he had children, all of them heads of households. And we do not know anyone narrated this hadith from Abu Sa'd except Ubaydullah ibn Musa."
"7534","7534 - And Ibrahim ibn Mujashshir narrated to us, Abidah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Sa'id Abu Sa'id, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: A group of Uraynah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and found the land unhealthy; their complexions turned yellow and their bellies swelled. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them to go to the charity camels and drink from their urine and milk. They recovered, then killed the herdsman and - I think he said - cast aside the camels. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seized them, cut off their hands and feet, and gouged - or branded - their eyes; Abidah doubted. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Abu Sa'd, from Anas, except Abidah ibn Humayd."
"7535","7535 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abu Sa'd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will keep asking about everything until they say: This is Allah, Mighty and Majestic, Who created everything, so who created Him?"
"7536","7536 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, Sa'id Abu Sa'd narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: A woman of the Ansar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. He said: If she sees that, let her wash. A'ishah said: O so-and-so, you have disgraced women. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave her, for the women of the Ansar ask about understanding of religion. Sa'id Abu Sa'd is Sa'id ibn al-Marzuban Abu Sa'd al-Baqqal, of the people of Kufa."
"7537","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla. 7537 - Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abdillah narrated to us, Husayn, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman, narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Anas, he said: Abu Talhah prepared about a mudd of food and ordered me - or said - sent me to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to invite him to the food. I came to him and said: Abu Talhah sent me to you for food he prepared. He said to the people: Stand. He said: I came hastening until I reached Abu Talhah. He said: What did you do? I said: I invited the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he invited the people. He said: You knew what we have, yet you disgraced us with the Messenger of Allah. I said: Yes, but I could not say anything to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, called ten, the people sat, placed the vessel before him, spoke what Allah, Blessed and Exalted, willed him to speak, then said to the people - I think he said - eat. They ate until full, then stood. Then he called ten, they ate until all the people ate, as I think, and there remained what sufficed his household."
"7538","7538 - Ishaq ibn Ziyad al-Ayli narrated it to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Sa'd Sa'id ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, from Anas, with something similar. And we do not know Ibn Abi Layla narrated from Anas except this hadith."
"7539","And al-Layth narrated it, from Khalid, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, from Anas. 7539 - And Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, from Anas, with something similar. And we do not know Muhammad ibn Ka'b narrated from Anas except this hadith."
"7540","7540 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you believes until Allah and His Messenger are more beloved to him than all else, and until being cast into the Fire is more beloved to him than returning to disbelief after Allah, Blessed and Exalted, saved him from it. No servant believes until I am more beloved to him than - and he mentioned something - his child and all people."
"7541","Talaq ibn Habib. 7541 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim related it to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, who said: I heard Talaq ibn Habib narrating from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it. And we do not know of Talaq ibn Habib narrating [musnad] from Anas except this hadith; and Talaq ibn Habib was a man from the people of Kufa who held the view of irja and was truthful in hadith."
"7542","Misahhaj al-Dabbi. 7542 - Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Misahhaj al-Dabbi, from Anas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped at a resting place, he would not depart from it until he had prayed in it."
"7543","7543 - Al-Sakan ibn Said narrated it to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from al-Misahhaj, from Anas, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham stopped while he was with al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf on one of his journeys, and he wanted to depart close to midday, so Anas said: What prevents you from praying before you depart, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he was at a resting place would pray in it before departing."
"7544","Hamzah al-Dabbi. 7544 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Hamzah al-Aidhi - who is Hamzah al-Dabbi - narrated to us, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped at a resting place, he would not depart until he prayed al-Zuhr. A man said: Even if it was midday? He said: Even if it was midday, meaning: he waits until the time."
"7545","7545 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Hamzah al-Dabbi, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: When we stopped at a resting place, we would not offer supererogatory prayer until the saddles were untied."
"7546","7546 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, who said: I heard Hamzah al-Dabbi, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: I never prayed behind any one man among the people whose prayer was lighter yet complete than the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And I think that Misahhaj al-Dabbi is Hamzah, but that is a nickname and Hamzah is the name."
"7547","Ismail ibn Salman. 7547 - Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Ismail ibn Salman al-Azraq narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Some birds were gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he divided them among his wives, and each wife received three of them; then in the morning he was with one of his wives, Safiyyah or another, and she brought them to him, so he said: O Allah, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to You to eat with me from this. I said: O Allah, make him a man from the Ansar. Then Ali - may Allah have mercy on him - came, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Anas, see who is at the door. I looked and there was Ali, so I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is occupied. Then I came and stood before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: See who is at the door. I looked and there was Ali, until he did that three times; then he entered walking while I was behind him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What kept you, may Allah have mercy on you? He said: This is the last of three times Anas turned me away, claiming you were occupied. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What made you do what you did? I said: O Messenger of Allah, I heard your supplication and I wanted him to be from my people. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may love his people, a man may love his people - he said it three times. And these words have been narrated from Anas through various chains, and everyone who narrated it from Anas is not strong; and Ismail ibn Salman is a man from the people of Kufa who narrated from Anas two hadiths, this hadith and another hadith."
"7548","7548 - Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated it to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: I was sitting with a man in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant believes until he loves for his Muslim brother what he loves for himself. Anas said: Then I and the man went out to the market, and there was merchandise being sold; I bargained with him and he said: For thirty. The man looked, so I said: I have taken it for forty. Its owner said: What makes you do this when I give it to you for less than this? Then he looked again, so I said: I have taken it for fifty. Its owner said: What makes you do this when I give it to you for less than this? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No servant believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself, and I consider it worth fifty."
"7549","Al-Amash from Anas. 7549 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Mamul al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rabiah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the privy, he would not raise his garment until he drew near to the ground."
"7550","7550 - Al-Sari ibn Asim narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Anas: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he needed to relieve himself would go far away."
"7551","7551 - Khalid ibn Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform ablution with the leftover water of his siwak. And this hadith was narrated by Sad ibn al-Salt, from al-Amash, from Salim, from Anas."
"7552","7552 - Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Anas ibn Malik: That he was asked about old women, did they attend prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, and the young women too."
"7553","7553 - And with the same chain: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man moving pebbles in prayer and said: That is your share of your prayer."
"7554","7554 - And with the same chain, and Yusuf ibn Musa related it to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, from Anas, and the wording is the wording of Khalid from his father, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Ramadan, so he fasted and his Companions fasted; then the call for Asr was made, so he broke his fast and some of his Companions broke fast with him while some of them continued fasting."
"7555","7555 - And with the same chain he said: The prayer would be established, then a man would intercept the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a need, and would detain him until some of the people dozed off."
"7556","7556 - And with the same chain: That Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf married a woman for the weight of a date-stone of gold."
"7557","7557 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Kufi narrated to us, Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Amash narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: A man from among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, and they said: Glad tidings of Paradise? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you not know? Perhaps he spoke about what did not concern him."
"7558","7558 - Ahmad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Umar ibn Hafs narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hands at Arafah supplicating, and the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is earnest supplication. Then the she-camel swerved, so he opened one of his hands and took hold of it while raising the other."
"7559","7559 - And al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, Abu Ismail al-Muaddib narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Anas: That a pregnant woman confessed to adultery four times, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Go back until you give birth. Then she came after she had delivered him, so he said: Nurse him until you wean him. Then she came and was stoned; then they mentioned her, and he said: She has repented a repentance that if the one who takes unlawful tax had repented it, he would have been forgiven. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Amash except Abu Ismail al-Muaddib."
"7560","7560 - Abdullah ibn Muawiyah al-Jumahi narrated to us, al-Rabi ibn Badr narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Anas, who said: Abu Taybah passed by us - I think he said after Asr - in Ramadan and said: I cupped the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Amash except al-Rabi ibn Badr, and al-Rabi is weak in hadith."
"7561","7561 - Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Anas, who said: I entered upon al-Hajjaj and said: I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for nine years, then he mentioned some speech that took place between them. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Amash except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash."
"7562","7562 - Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Haddadi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to the owner on account of the owned, and woe to the owned on account of the owner, and woe to the rich on account of the poor, and woe to the poor on account of the rich, and woe to the strong on account of the weak, and woe to the weak on account of the strong. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Amash except Abu Shihab."
"7563","7563 - Muhammad ibn al-Layth narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Bashir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting under a tree, then the tree moved, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up frightened; he was asked about that and said: I thought it was the Hour, or as he said. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Amash except Ahmad ibn Bashir."
"7564","7564 - Ismail ibn Masud narrated to us, as far as I know, Aththam ibn Ali narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Anas - I think he raised it - who said: The muezzins will be the longest-necked of people on the Day of Resurrection."
"7565","7565 - Rizqullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himmani narrated to us, from al-Amash, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying regarding the statement of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: {and more upright in speech}: He said: And more truthful. It was said to him: It is recited as ""and more upright""; so he said: More upright and more truthful are one. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Amash except Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani."
"7566","7566 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, who said: I saw Anas ibn Malik praying in Makkah, and when he prostrated he spread his arms until I saw the wrinkles of his armpits. And I mentioned these two raised hadiths from al-Amash, from Anas, only to clarify that al-Amash had heard from Anas; and it is said: he only narrated them from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So if he had seen Anas and heard from him, what he sent [as mursal] is not denied; and it is possible that he heard some of them, or heard them except for what he inserted between him and Anas therein a man."
"7567","Ibrahim al-Taymi. 7567 - Muadh ibn Shubah narrated to us, Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, from Abu al-Haytham, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When food is brought near to one of you while on his feet are sandals, let him remove his sandals, for it is more restful for the feet."
"7568","7568 - Abdullah ibn Said al-Kindi narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from his father, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you sit, take off your sandals - I think he said: your feet will rest. And these words, we do not know of anyone who narrated them except Anas."
"7569","Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhtah. 7569 - Sahl ibn Bahr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhtah, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dates and raisins being mixed together for nabidh. And we do not know of Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhtah narrating [musnad] from Anas except this hadith."
"7570","Habib ibn Abi Thabit. 7570 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, Tumah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Habib - meaning Ibn Abi Thabit - from Anas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever prays forty days - I think he said in congregation - there is written for him a clearance from the Fire and a clearance from hypocrisy. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Anas except through this chain, and we do not know of anyone who narrated from Habib except Tumah ibn Amr al-Jafari; and Habib narrated from Anas three hadiths, one of them this, and the other:"
"7571","7571 - Humayd ibn al-Rabi narrated it to us, Firdaws ibn al-Ashari narrated to us, from Masud ibn Sulayman, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Anas: That a man said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I bequeath all my wealth? He said: No. He said: Then half? He said: No. He said: Then a third? He said: A third, and a third is much. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from Anas except through this chain."
"7572","7572 - And he narrated another hadith which Abu al-Ala Khalid ibn Tahman narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Anas: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The rulers are from Quraysh, and this affair will remain among you. 7573 - Ahmad ibn al-Mualla narrated it to us, al-Hasan ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Abu al-Ala al-Khaffaf, from Habib, from Anas."
"7573","Muslim al-Awar. 7574 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Muslim al-Awar, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Khaybar upon a donkey whose bridle was of palm fiber."
"7574","7575 - And with the same chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would visit the sick, follow the funeral, ride the donkey, and accept the invitation of the slave. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Anas except Muslim al-Awar; and a group narrated it from Muslim: Ibn Uyaynah and Shubah and others, so we sufficed with Shubah."
"7575","7576 - Muadh ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Muslim, from Anas: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a tray upon which were unripe dates and ripe dates, and he would eat the ripe dates and leave the overripe ones with tails."
"7576","7577 - Muadh ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Muslim, from Anas, raising it: When the People of the Book greet you, say: Upon you, or: And upon you."
"7577","Amr ibn Amir. 7578 - Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Misar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Amr ibn Amir, from Anas ibn Malik."
"7578","7579 - And Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Ubaydah al-Usfuri narrated it to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Amr ibn Amir, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and did not wrong anyone his wage. And the wording is the wording of Misar; and we do not know of Abu al-Zinad narrating [musnad] from Amr ibn Amir other than this hadith."
"7579","7580 - Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Muslim narrated to us, from Anas: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave Khaybar [to be worked] for half."
"7580","Burayd ibn Abi Maryam. 7581 - Zayd ibn Akhzam Abu Talib al-Tai narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Hunai narrated to us, Humayd ibn Mihran narrated to us, from Abu al-Zibriqan al-Hilali, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas ibn Malik: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: {Say: He is Allah, the One} equals a third of the Quran."
"7581","7582 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas."
"7582","7583 - And I heard Abu al-Hasan al-Qazzaz narrating from Abu Dawud, from Sallam Abu al-Ahwas, from Abu Ishaq, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks Paradise three times, Paradise says: O Allah, admit him to Paradise; and whoever seeks refuge from the Fire three times, the Fire says: O Allah, grant him refuge from the Fire."
"7583","7584 - Amr narrated to us, Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7584","7585 - And Abdullah ibn al-Sabbah al-Attar related it to us, Abu Ali al-Hanafi narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas ibn Malik: That the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Supplication between the adhan and the iqamah is not rejected. And this hadith was narrated by a group from Anas, among them al-Taymi and others."
"7585","7586 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Khalid ibn al-Fizr, from Anas ibn Malik: That the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Muzzat is unlawful, meaning a mixture of unripe dates and [dry] dates."
"7586","7587 - Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Haddadi narrated to us, Ubaydullah Musa narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Khalid ibn al-Fizr, from Anas ibn Malik: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he dispatched an expedition would say: Wage war in the name of Allah and in the path of Allah; fight those who disbelieve in Allah; do not mutilate, and do not kill a child. And Khalid ibn al-Fizr, we do not know of anyone who narrated from him except al-Hasan ibn Salih, and we do not know of him narrating from Anas except these two hadiths."
"7587","Bayan Abu Bishr. 7588 - Khalid ibn Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Bayan Abu Bishr, from Anas ibn Malik: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a wedding feast for Safiyyah. And we do not know of Bayan narrating from Anas except this hadith; and a group narrated it from Bayan, so we sufficed with Abu Awanah."
"7588","7589 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Asamm, from Anas."
"7589","7590 - And Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil related it to us, saying: My grandfather Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated to me, Hammam narrated to us, from Layth, from Abd al-Rahman al-Asamm, from Anas ibn Malik - and the wording is the wording of Hammam - that he prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman; all of them would say takbir when prostrating and when rising."
"7590","7591 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Asamm, from Anas: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Umar a gift of silk, so he returned it; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you return it? I only sent it to you so that you sell it and benefit from it."
"7591","Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay. 7592 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, who said: I asked Anas ibn Malik and said to him: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray Zuhr on the day of Tarwiyah? He said: At Mina. I said: Then where did he pray Asr on the day of sacrifice? He said: At al-Abtah. Then he said afterwards: As your rulers do. And we do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Ishaq al-Azraq; and we do not know of Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay narrating [musnad] from Anas except this hadith."
"7592","7593 - And a hadith which Khalid ibn Tahir ibn Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, from his father, from Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Take sahur, for in sahur there is blessing. And he was not followed in this hadith; and he only meant Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb as we see."
"7593","Abd al-Warith. 7594 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abd al-Warith, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four will be brought on the Day of Resurrection: the newborn, the imbecile, one who died in the fatrah, and the decrepit old man; each of them will speak his plea. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will say to a neck of Hell - I think he said: Come forth - and He will say to them: I used to send to My servants messengers from among themselves, and I am My own messenger to you: enter this. Then whoever was decreed wretched will say: O Lord, do You enter us into it when from it we used to flee? And whoever was decreed felicity will proceed and plunge into it hastening. He said: Then Allah will say: You have disobeyed Me, and you are more severe in denying and disobeying My messengers. He said: Then He will admit these to Paradise and admit these to the Fire."
"7594","7595 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Mukhtar ibn Abi Mukhtar, from Abd al-Warith, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The newborn is in Paradise, and the buried infant girl is in Paradise; and he mentioned a third which escaped me."
"7595","7596 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Bashir, from Anas ibn Malik, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), regarding the statement of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: {By your Lord, We will surely question them all, about what they used to do}. He said: About La ilaha illa Allah. And Bashir, we do not know of anyone who narrated from him except Layth ibn Abi Sulaym."
"7596","7597 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Layth, from Bashir, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace be upon him), likewise."
"7597","7598 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Ismail narrated to us, Harb ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Zuhayr, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Spending in the path of Allah is multiplied to seven hundredfold. And we do not know of Yazid ibn Zuhayr narrating from Anas except this hadith."
"7598","Husayn ibn Abi Sufyan. 7599 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abi Sufyan, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw Umm Sulaym praying in her house and said: O Umm Sulaym, when you have prayed the obligatory prayer, say: Subhan Allah ten times, and al-hamdu lillah ten times, and Allahu Akbar ten times; then ask whatever you wish, for He will say to you: Yes, yes, yes - three times. And we do not know of anyone who narrated from Husayn ibn Abi Sufyan except Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, and he narrated from him only two hadiths; he raised one of them in isnad, and it is this."
"7599","And the other: Abu Talhah would begin the morning fasting voluntarily, then come to his family and say: Do you have anything. 7600 - Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated it to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Husayn, from Anas."
"7600","Salim ibn Abi al-Jad. 7601 - Salih ibn Adi ibn Abi Imarah al-Zari narrated to us, al-Sumaydih ibn Wahb narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur and Amr ibn Murrah, both saying: Salim ibn Abi al-Jad narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: That a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when is the Hour? He said: What have you prepared for it? He said: I have not prepared much for it except that I love Allah and His Messenger. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man is with whom he loves. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Shubah, from Amr and Mansur, from Salim, from Anas, except al-Sumaydih; and others than al-Sumaydih narrated it from Shubah, from Mansur alone, from Salim, from Anas."
"7601","Sulayman and Abd al-Aziz and Hammad and Attab. 7602 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi and Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb and Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman and Attab the freed slave of Hurmuz, from Anas: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. And we do not know of anyone who gathered those we mentioned from Anas except Shubah; and we do not know of it being narrated from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman except by Shubah."
"7602","7603 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Attab the freed slave of Hurmuz, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I pledged allegiance to the Prophet (peace be upon him) to hear and obey as much as I could. And we do not know of anyone who narrated from Attab the freed slave of Hurmuz except Shubah; he narrated from him two hadiths."
"7603","Amr ibn Suwayd. 7604 - Humayd ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, Dirar ibn Surad narrated to us, al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Umar ibn Suwayd, from Anas, who said: The door of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would be knocked with fingernails."
"7604","Talhah ibn Musarrif. 7605 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, Yazid ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a date on the road and said: Were it not that I fear it is from charity, I would have eaten it. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Talhah ibn Musarrif except Mansur; and we do not know that Talhah narrated from Anas other than this hadith."
"7605","7606 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Israil, from al-Suddi, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: There were orphans in the care of Abu Talhah, and he bought wine for them; then when the prohibition of wine came down, he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: Shall I make it vinegar? He said: No, so he poured it out. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Anas except Yahya ibn Abbad; al-Suddi narrated it from him, and Qays narrated it from al-Suddi, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from Anas, from Abu Talhah; and al-Thawri narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Anas."
"7606","7607 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Haysam narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Yafur, who said: I asked Anas about wiping over the khuffs, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wipe over them. And we do not know of Abu Yafur narrating from Anas other than this hadith."
"7607","7608 - Ahmad ibn Sinan narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Suddi, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from Anas, who said: Abu Talhah had wine belonging to orphans; then when the prohibition of wine came down, that was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Pour it out."
"7608","7609 - Yusuf narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from Anas, likewise. End of the eighth part of the Musnad of Anas, may Allah have mercy on him, and praise be to Allah."
"7609","What Ibn Abbas narrated from Abu Hurayrah. 7610 - Muhammad ibn Attab narrated to us, saying: Abu Ayyub Sulayman ibn Khalaf narrated to us, saying: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mufarrij narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib al-Raqqi informed us, saying: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq narrated to us, saying: Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, saying: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, from Abu Hurayrah: That a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw as if a canopy dripping ghee and honey, and the people between taking much and taking little; and there was a rope extending from the heaven to the earth. You came, O Messenger of Allah, and took hold of it and rose, and Allah raised you. Then another man took hold of it and rose with it. Then another man took hold of it and rose with it. Then another man took hold of it, and it broke with him, then it was joined for him and he rose with it. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, let me interpret it. He said: Interpret it. He said: As for the canopy, it is the canopy of Islam; and as for what drips of ghee and honey, it is the Quran and its sweetness; and as for those taking much and little, they are those who take much of the Quran and those who take little; and as for the rope extending from the heaven to the earth, it is the truth upon which you are - so take hold of it and Allah will raise you. Then after you a man will take hold of it and rise with it. Then after him another man will take hold of it and rise with it. Then another man will take hold of it and it will break, then it will be joined for him and he will rise; O Messenger of Allah, tell me: did I get it right or wrong? He said: You got part right and part wrong. He said: I adjure you, O Messenger of Allah, tell me what I got wrong. He said: Do not swear. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who said: from Ubaydullah, from Ibn Abbas, from Abu Hurayrah, except..."
"7610","7611 - Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, saying: Mamar informed us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that he was asked about lamam and said: I find in it nothing except what Abu Hurayrah said from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The adultery of the eye is looking, the adultery of the hand is grasping, and the adultery of the foot is walking. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Ibn Abbas, from Abu Hurayrah, except Mamar; and others than Mamar narrated it from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah. Thus said Wahb; and Warqa said: from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, and did not say: from Abu Hurayrah."
"7611","7612 - Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam al-Ijli narrated to us, saying: Al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Mamar narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever catches a rakah of Asr prayer before the sun sets, or a rakah of Fajr prayer before the sun rises, has caught it. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it except Mamar; and he raised it in isnad from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from Abu Hurayrah; and these words have been narrated from Abu Hurayrah through various chains."
"7612","7613 - Al-Abbas ibn Jafar al-Baghdadi and Salih ibn Muadh narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Jawwab al-Ahwas ibn Jawwab narrated to us, saying: Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: In Friday there is an hour which no Muslim meets asking Allah therein for good except He gives it to him. And this hadith was narrated by others than Ammar ibn Ruzayq, from Mansur, from Mujahid, who said: Abu Hurayrah and Kab differed, then he mentioned it from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah; and none inserted Ibn Abbas between them except in the hadith of Ammar ibn Ruzayq."
"7613","7614 - Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, who said: Abdullah ibn Abi Husayn narrated to me, saying: Nafi ibn Jubayr narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Musaylimah the liar came in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he came to Madinah and began saying: If Muhammad assigns the authority after him to me, I will follow him. He came to it with a group of his people. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came toward him, and with him was Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas; and in the hand of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a piece of palm stalk, until he stood over Musaylimah - may the curse of Allah be upon him and his companions. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: If you asked me for this piece, I would not give it to you, and you will not go beyond Allah's decree concerning you; and I see for you what I was shown, and this is Thabit ibn Qays who will answer you on my behalf; and he turned away from him. Ibn Abbas said: Then I asked about the statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Ibn Abbas said: Then I asked about the statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I show you what I saw, or the dream I saw concerning you. He said: Abu Hurayrah informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While he was sleeping, he said: I saw in my hands two bracelets of gold, and it was revealed to me in the dream: Blow them. So I blew them and they flew away; and I interpreted them as al-Ansi and the other as Musaylimah, the companion of Yamamah. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Ibn Abbas, from Abu Hurayrah, except through this chain; and we do not know of it being narrated with this wording except through this chain with this isnad."
"7614","What Anas narrated from Abu Hurayrah. 7615 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, saying: Al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Anas, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When the servant draws near to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, a handspan, Allah draws near to him a cubit; and when he draws near to Him a cubit, He draws near to him a fathom. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Anas, from Abu Hurayrah, except al-Mutamir from his father; and it has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah through other chains, and from others than Abu Hurayrah as well."
"7615","7616 - Al-Hasan ibn Yahya and Ibrahim ibn al-Mutamir narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Habib narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw Musa praying in his grave on the night I was taken up. And this hadith has been narrated from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and we do not know of anyone who said: from Anas, from Abu Hurayrah, except Umar ibn Habib, from al-Taymi, from Anas; and Umar was not a preserver."
"7616","7617 - Al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, saying: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for Paradise, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will create for it a creation - meaning: then He will settle them in it. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it except Thabit, from Anas, from Abu Hurayrah; and the companions of Hammad shortened it, making it from Thabit, from Anas."
"7617","What Jabir narrated from Abu Hurayrah. 7618 - Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, saying: Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ayan narrated to us, saying: Maqil - meaning Ibn Ubaydullah al-Jazari - narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade urinating in stagnant water and then performing ablution from it or bathing. And we do not know of Jabir narrating from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith, and a hadith which Ibn Luhayah also narrated from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from Abu Hurayrah."
"7618","7619 - Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Ibn Luhayah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you wakes from his sleep, let him not dip his hand into the vessel until he washes it."
"7619","Abu Ayyub from Abu Hurayrah. 7620 - Ibrahim ibn Bistam al-Zafarani narrated to us, saying: Said ibn Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha, from his father, from Abu Ayyub; and Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Khallab narrated it to us, saying: Yahya ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, from Shubah, from Ashath, from his father, who said: I came to Madinah and found Abu Ayyub narrating from Abu Hurayrah, so I said: You narrate from Abu Hurayrah though you saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?! He said: He heard."
"7620","Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah from Abu Hurayrah. 7621 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Abu Amir Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from al-Jahm ibn Abi al-Jahm, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has placed the truth upon the tongue of Umar and his heart. And we do not know of al-Miswar ibn Makhramah narrating [musnad] from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith; and we do not know for it a path except this path from al-Miswar."
"7621","Abu Said ibn al-Mualla from Abu Hurayrah. 7622 - Abd al-Samad ibn Sulayman al-Marwazi narrated to us, saying: Abu Nubatah narrated to us, saying: Salamah ibn Wardan narrated to us, from Abu Said ibn al-Mualla, from Ali ibn Abi Talib and Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: What is between my grave and my minbar is a garden from the gardens of Paradise; and a prayer in my mosque is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere except al-Masjid al-Haram."
"7622","7623 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, saying: Abu Shaybah Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Shaybah narrated to us, saying: Abu Nubatah Yunus ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Wardan, from Abu Said ibn al-Mualla, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: My close friend enjoined upon me three: not to sleep except upon witr, fasting three days of every month, and ghusl on Friday, if Allah wills. And we do not know of Abu Said ibn al-Mualla narrating [musnad] from Abu Hurayrah except these two hadiths; and Abu Said ibn al-Mualla is among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he narrated other than hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he narrated from the Prophet two hadiths, one of them the change of the qiblah, and the other: Do not leave the mosque until I teach you."
"7623","What Qabisah ibn Dhuayb narrated from Abu Hurayrah. 7624 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, saying: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade marrying a woman together with her paternal aunt and together with her maternal aunt. And this hadith was narrated by more than one from al-Zuhri, from Qabisah; and it was narrated from Abu Hurayrah through other chains."
"7624","7625 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, saying: Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Black banners will come out from the direction of the east."
"7625","7626 - And Said ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, saying: Uthman ibn Ata al-Khurasani narrated to us, from his father, from Ishaq ibn Qabisah ibn Dhuayb, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah: That he said: He and Zayd ibn Thabit differed concerning the Quran."
"7626","Abu Umamah ibn Sahl from Abu Hurayrah. 7627 - Yahya ibn Hakim and Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, saying: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, saying: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah and Abu Umamah ibn Sahl, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announced the death of al-Najashi on the day he died and said: A brother of yours has died, so pray over him. And he went out with the people to the prayer ground and prayed, and they formed rows behind him, and he said takbir over him four takbirs. And we do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith from Said and Abu Salamah and Abu Umamah, from Abu Hurayrah, except Uthman ibn Umar, from Yunus."
"7627","7628 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, saying: Said ibn Ufayr narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Qays ibn Salim, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: We said to him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What would people fear when they entered a town or overlooked a town, that they would say: O Allah, grant us therein provision and residence? He said: They used to fear the injustice of rulers and the withholding of rain. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it except Abu Hurayrah; and we do not know for it a path except this path from Abu Hurayrah."
"7628","7629 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq ibn Bukayr and Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, saying in their hadith: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, Said ibn Salamah narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Jubayr informed me, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lowest of the people of Paradise in fortune or share are a people whom Allah will bring out of the Fire, and the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, will rest for them - they had not associated anything with Allah. They will appear in the open and grow as vegetation grows, until when the spirits enter their bodies, they will say: Our Lord who brought us out of the Fire and returned the spirits to our bodies, turn our faces away from the Fire. He said: Then He will turn their faces away from the Fire."
"7629","7630 - Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Sakan narrated to us, Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Ubaydullah narrated to me, saying: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A [good] dream is from Allah and a bad dream is from Satan; so when one of you sees what he dislikes, let him spit to his left and seek refuge with Allah from its evil, and it will not harm him. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Abu Umamah, except Salih."
"7630","7631 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Mamar ibn Busr narrated to us, saying: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Hasten with the funeral; if it was righteous, you advance it to good, and if it was other than that, it is an evil you cast off from your necks. And this hadith was narrated by others than Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah."
"7631","What Said ibn al-Musayyib narrated from Abu Hurayrah. 7632 - Muhammad ibn Ziyad and Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us - and the wording is Muhammad's - saying: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When the heat intensifies, cool down with prayer, for the intensity of heat is from the exhalation of Hell."
"7632","7633 - Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jurayj informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: When the heat intensifies, cool down with prayer - meaning Zuhr prayer - for the intensity of heat is from the exhalation of Hell."
"7633","7634 - And al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), likewise."
"7634","7635 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about prayer in a single garment and said: Does every one of you find two garments."
"7635","7636 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see the crescent, fast; and when you see it, break fast; and if it is obscured for you, fast thirty days."
"7636","7637 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you wakes from his sleep, let him not put his hand into the vessel until he washes it, for he does not know - I think he said - where his hand spent the night. And this hadith was narrated by Ibn Uyaynah and others from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah; and Mamar joined Said and Abu Salamah."
"7637","7638 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, saying: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been aided with awe, and given the comprehensive words; and while I was sleeping, the keys of the treasures of the earth were brought and placed in my hand. Abu Hurayrah said: Then the Messenger of Allah went, and you are extracting them. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, except Mamar."
"7638","7639 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you leads people in prayer, let him lighten, for among them are the sick, the very old, and the one with a need."
"7639","7640 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The [injury by a] stray animal is not compensated, the mine is not compensated, the well is not compensated, and in buried treasure is a fifth."
"7640","7641 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone."
"7641","7642 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announced the death of al-Najashi to the people while he was in Madinah, and prayed over him and said takbir four times."
"7642","7643 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The congregational prayer exceeds the prayer of a man alone by some twenty - I think he said: degrees."
"7643","7644 - Ahmad ibn al-Faraj al-Himsi narrated to us, saying: Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated to us, saying: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Said ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: When the reciter says amin, say amin; for the imam says amin, and the angels say amin. So whoever's amin coincides with the angels' amin, what preceded of his sin is forgiven."
"7644","7645 - And Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Sadusi narrated it to us, saying: Rawh narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Hafsah - meaning Muhammad - narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), likewise."
"7645","7646 - Fahm ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, saying: Sufyan - meaning Ibn Uyaynah - narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7646","7647 - And Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated it to us, saying: Sufyan informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, raising it, who said: Tasbih is for men and clapping is for women."
"7647","7648 - And Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Sadusi and Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, saying: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Tasbih is for men and clapping is for women."
"7648","7649 - Al-Fadl ibn Yaqub al-Rukhami narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, saying: Al-Awzai narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah and Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Jews and Christians do not dye, so differ from them. And this hadith was narrated by Ibn Uyaynah and Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah and Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah; and al-Awzai said: from Said and Abu Salamah and Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah."
"7649","7650 - Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, saying: Al-Awzai narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salamah and Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah and Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer when he commits adultery, nor steal while he is a believer when he steals, nor drink wine while he is a believer when he drinks it. And this hadith, I do not know of anyone who gathered therein Said and Abu Salamah and Ubaydullah and Humayd except al-Awzai, nor from him except Muhammad ibn Kathir."
"7650","7651 - Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Bahrani narrated to us, saying: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, saying: Yunus - meaning Ibn Yazid - narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Two women from Hudhayl fought, and one of them threw a stone at the other and killed her and what was in her womb. They disputed about the blood money to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: The blood money of her fetus is a slave or slave-girl; and he decreed the blood money upon her kin, and made her child inherit from her. Hamal ibn Malik said: How do I pay for one who neither drank nor ate, nor spoke nor cried, and the like of that is wasted? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is only from the brothers of soothsayers - because of the rhymed speech he rhymed."
"7651","7652 - And Ahmad ibn al-Faraj al-Himsi narrated to us, saying: Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated to us, saying: Yunus - meaning Ibn Yazid - narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Friday there is an hour which no Muslim meets while praying except he is answered; and he belittled it and made little of it. And we do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith from Said and Abu Salamah except Ayyub, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri."
"7652","7653 - And Ahmad ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, saying: Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated to us, saying: Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Abu Salamah and Ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman and Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah said that Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr or Asr and gave salam after two rakahs. Dhu al-Shimalayn ibn Umar ibn Nadlah al-Khuzai - an ally of Banu Zuhrah - said to him: Has the prayer been shortened or did you forget, O Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah turned to the people and said: Is Dhu al-Shimalayn truthful? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah stood and completed the prayer, and prostrated two prostrations while sitting. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who gathered this group therein from al-Zuhri except Yunus. And al-Awzai narrated it from al-Zuhri, from three of these, from Abu Hurayrah."
"7653","7654 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, saying: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: An ant bit a prophet among the prophets, so he ordered the ant village and it was burned; then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed to him: That an ant bit you, you destroyed a nation among nations that glorify."
"7654","7655 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, saying: Yunus narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The heart of the old man is young in love of wealth and long hope."
"7655","7656 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, saying: Yunus narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do not withhold surplus water to withhold thereby herbage."
"7656","7657 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, saying: Yunus narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished Fajr prayer and bowed and raised his head, he would say: Allah hears him who praises Him; O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise. Save al-Walid ibn al-Walid and Salamah ibn Hisham and Ayyash ibn Abi Rabiah and the oppressed among the believers. O Allah, make severe Your grip upon Mudar, and make it upon them years like the years of Yusuf."
"7657","7658 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Al-Layth narrated to me, saying: Yunus narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, who said: Said and Abu Salamah narrated to me that Abu Hurayrah used to narrate that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: What I have forbidden you, avoid it; and what I have commanded you, do of it as much as you can; for those before you were destroyed only by their many questions and their differing with their prophets."
"7658","7659 - Muhammad ibn Miskin ibn Numaylah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not trade dates until their soundness appears, and do not trade dates for dates."
"7659","7660 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Yunus - meaning Ibn Yazid - narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, who said: Abu Salamah and Said said, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While a man was driving a cow of his which he had loaded, the cow turned to him and said: I was not created for this; I was only created for plowing. The people said: Subhan Allah!! In amazement: A cow speaking?! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I believe in it, I and Abu Bakr and Umar."
"7660","7661 - Zayd ibn Akhzam Abu Talib narrated to us, saying: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are more deserving of doubt than Ibrahim when he said: {My Lord, show me how You give life to the dead. He said: Do you not believe? He said: Yes, but that my heart may be at rest}. And may Allah have mercy on Lut; he would indeed have resorted to a strong support. And this hadith was narrated by Abu Uways, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Ubayd, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7661","7661/2 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated it to us with it, saying: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Abu Uways narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Ubayd, from Abu Hurayrah."
"7662","7662 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, saying: Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr ibn Uways narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Yahya ibn Said, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever catches a rakah of prayer has caught the whole prayer, except that he makes up what he missed."
"7663","7663 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, saying: Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Yahya ibn Said, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you say to your companion: Be silent, you have engaged in idle talk - meaning on Friday."
"7664","7664 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, saying: Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Yahya ibn Said, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When the prayer is established, do not come to it running; come to it walking, with tranquility upon you. What you catch, pray; and what you miss, make up."
"7665","7665 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, saying: Ayyub ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he said: Allah hears him who praises Him, would say: Our Lord, to You is praise; then he would say: Allahu Akbar - when falling prostrate."
"7666","7666 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Al-Layth narrated to me, saying: Uqayl - meaning Ibn Khalid - narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, who said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman and Said ibn al-Musayyib narrated to me that Abu Hurayrah informed them that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: In the black seed there is healing for every disease except death. And this hadith was narrated by Ibn Uyaynah, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah."
"7667","7667 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Al-Layth narrated to me, saying: Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, who said: Said and Abu Salamah narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A man from the Muslims came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in the mosque and called him, saying: O Messenger of Allah, I have committed adultery. He turned away from him until he heard that four times. When he testified against himself four testimonies, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and said: Are you married? He said: Yes. So he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take him and stone him."
"7668","7668 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Al-Layth narrated to me, saying: Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, who said: Said and Abu Salamah narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While a shepherd was among his sheep, a wolf attacked them and took a sheep from them; the shepherd pursued it until he rescued it from him. The wolf turned to him and said: Who will guard it on the day of beasts, the day when there is no shepherd but me? The people said: Subhan Allah!! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I believe in that, I and Abu Bakr and Umar. And this hadith, we preserve it only from the hadith of Uqayl, from al-Zuhri."
"7669","7669 - Muhammad ibn Miskin ibn Numaylah narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Al-Layth narrated to me, saying: Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, who said: Said ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salamah narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah: That he said: I heard a man ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Does one of us pray in a single garment? He said: Does every one of you find two garments."
"7670","7670 - Muhammad ibn Miskin and Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, from al-Layth, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid - meaning Ibn Musafir - narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah and Said, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: By Him in whose hand is my soul, were it not that men from the Muslims dislike staying behind me, and I do not find what to carry them on, I would not stay behind any expedition fighting in the path of Allah. By Him in whose hand is my soul, I would love to be killed in the path of Allah, then brought to life, then killed, then brought to life, then killed."
"7671","7671 - Muhammad ibn Miskin and Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The example of the mujahid in the path of Allah - and Allah knows best who strives in His path - is like the example of one fasting and standing; and Allah has undertaken - or he said: Allah has guaranteed - for whoever strives in His path to take his soul and admit him to Paradise, or return him safe with what he obtained of reward and booty."
"7672","7672 - Umar ibn al-Khattab and Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Al-Layth narrated to me, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, who said: Said ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salamah narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade uninterrupted fasting. A man from the Muslims said: But you, O Messenger of Allah, fast uninterruptedly? The Messenger of Allah said: Which of you is like me? I spend the night with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink. When they refused to stop uninterrupted fasting, he fasted uninterruptedly with them a day, then a day; then they saw the crescent, so he said: Had it been delayed, I would have continued with you - as a deterrent for them, meaning when they refused to stop."
"7673","7673 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, saying: Abu Amir narrated to us, saying: Zamah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, who heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not make nabidh in gourds and pitch-coated vessels - or he said: naqir. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, except Zamah."
"7674","7674 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, saying: Abu Amir Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, saying: Zamah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hasten with your funerals; if it was good, it is good you advance; and if it was evil, you cast it off from your necks. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Said and Abu Salamah except Zamah, from al-Zuhri."
"7675","7675 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Himsi narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Salim narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi - whose name is Muhammad ibn al-Walid - from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A scholar from the Jews came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, into what will the food of the people of Paradise turn? He said: It will become sweat like beads of musk."
"7676","7676 - Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, saying: Shuayb - meaning Ibn Abi Hamzah - narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Said ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood when there was revealed to him: {And warn your nearest kin}. He said: Purchase yourselves from Allah; I avail you nothing against Allah. O Banu Abd Manaf, I avail you nothing against Allah. O Safiyyah bint Abd al-Muttalib, I avail you nothing against Allah. O Fatimah bint Muhammad, I avail you nothing against Allah; ask me of my wealth what you wish. O Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, I avail you nothing against Allah. And this hadith was narrated from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah: Yunus and Shuayb; and the known one is from the hadith of Shuayb."
"7677","7677 - Muhammad ibn Mamar and Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Five are from the fitrah: circumcision, shaving the pubes, plucking the armpit, trimming the nails, and clipping the mustache."
"7678","7678 - And Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, saying: Rawh narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do not call it karm; for karm is the heart of the believer. And this hadith was narrated by Ibn Uyaynah, from al-Zuhri, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah."
"7679","7679 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, saying: Rawh narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A Bedouin entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting; he prayed two rakahs, then said: Have mercy on me and Muhammad, and have mercy on no one with us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have narrowed something wide. Then he did not remain long before he urinated in a corner of the mosque; the people hastened to him, so he forbade them and said: You were only sent as facilitators and were not sent as causers of hardship. Pour a bucket of water, or a water skin of water - meaning: in the place. And this hadith was narrated by Sufyan, from al-Zuhri, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah."
"7680","7680 - Muhammad ibn Mamar and Ahmad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, saying: Rawh narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do not revile time; for Allah is time, Blessed and Exalted."
"7681","7681 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qatii narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Qays narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever catches a rakah of Friday prayer, let him add another to it. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, except Umar ibn Qays alone; and Umar is weak in hadith, and there is only written from his hadith what he is alone in, of what others did not share with him."
"7682","7682 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Qays narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever has three die for him will not enter the Fire - or he said: The Fire will not touch him except to fulfill the oath. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, except Umar ibn Qays; and we already mentioned him, and Malik and Ibn Uyaynah and others narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah."
"7683","7683 - Al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Ubaydullah narrated to us, saying: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I have been commanded to fight people until they say La ilaha illa Allah. Umar said to Abu Bakr: How do you fight people when they say La ilaha illa Allah? He said: If they withheld from me a tether of what they used to give to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I would fight them for it. And this hadith, some said it from Abu Hurayrah, from Umar; and some said from Abu Hurayrah; and more than one narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Abu Hurayrah."
"7684","7684 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, saying: Shuayb narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: That a man from the Muslims saw a man from the Jews, and the Muslim said: By Him who chose Muhammad over mankind. The Jew said: By Him who chose Musa over mankind, so the Muslim slapped him. The Jew came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of the Muslim's deed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prefer me over Musa; for people will fall unconscious on the Day of Resurrection, and I will be the first to raise my head; then I will find him under a leg of the Throne, and I will not know whether he fell unconscious among those who fell unconscious and woke, or was among those whom Allah exempted.... And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Said and Abu Salamah except Shuayb; and al-Numan ibn Rashid and others narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7685","7685 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us with the hadith of al-Numan, saying: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, from his father, from al-Numan, from al-Zuhri, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7686","7686 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Majishun narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id and Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7687","7687 - Al-Sakan ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Malik, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id and Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he ruled for pre-emption in what had not been divided, and when the boundaries fall then there is no pre-emption. And the wording is that of Abd al-Malik. And this hadith Malik narrated in al-Muwatta from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id and Abu Salama, mursal, and Ma'mar narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salama, from Jabir."
"7688","7688 - Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, he said: Anbasa ibn Mihran narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id and Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Disputation about the Qur'an is disbelief. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id and Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, except Anbasa, and he is a man who is not strong, and concerning it he has another isnad."
"7689","7689 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb, meaning Ibn Abi Hamza, narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayra, he said: You say Abu Hurayra narrates much from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and you say: what is it with the Muhajirun and Ansar that they do not narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) like the hadith of Abu Hurayra? My brothers among the Muhajirun were kept busy by trading in the markets, and my brothers among the Ansar were kept busy by working their properties, and I was a poor man among the poor of al-Suffa, serving the Messenger of Allah for the fill of my stomach, so I would attend when they were absent and remember when they forgot, and he said to me in a hadith he was narrating: there is no one who spreads his garment until I finish this speech of mine, then gathers it to himself, except that he will retain what I say, so I spread a striped cloak that was on me until when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his speech I gathered it to my chest, and I did not forget anything of that speech of the Messenger of Allah. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id and Abu Salama, except Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamza."
"7690","7690 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman and Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib narrated to me, they heard Abu Hurayra saying: A man from Aslam came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in the mosque and called him and said: O Messenger of Allah, the other has committed zina, meaning himself, so he turned away from him, then he moved to the side of his face toward which he had turned, and said: O Messenger of Allah, the other has committed zina, so he turned away from him, then he moved to the side of his face from which he had turned away, and said: O Messenger of Allah, the other has committed zina, so he turned away from him, then he moved to one side of the face, and when he bore witness against himself four testimonies, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and said: Is there madness in you? He said: No, so he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take him away and stone him, and he had been married. And this hadith others besides Shu'ayb have narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id and Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, and Shu'ayb has the best wording of it."
"7691","7691 - Muhammad ibn Ziyad and Ahmad ibn Abda narrated to us, and the wording is Muhammad's, from Sufyan ibn Uyayna, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Fire complained to its Lord and said: O Lord, parts of me have eaten others, so He permitted it two breaths, a breath in winter and a breath in summer, so the most severe heat is from the exhalation of Hell, and the most severe bitter cold is from the cold of Hell."
"7692","7692 - Muhammad ibn Ziyad and Ahmad ibn Abda narrated to us, and the wording is Muhammad's, from Sufyan, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Saddles are not tied except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, and this mosque of mine, and al-Aqsa Mosque."
"7693","7693 - Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, he said: A man from Banu Fazara came and said: O Messenger of Allah, my wife has given birth to a black boy! The Prophet said: Do you have camels? He said: Yes, he said: What are their colors? He said: Red, he said: Is there any grey among them? He said: Yes, among them are grey ones. He said: What is its case? He said: Perhaps a strain pulled it! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And this one, perhaps a strain pulled him. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except from this angle with this isnad."
"7694","7694 (m) - Ali ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The earth was made for me a mosque and a purification. And this hadith we heard only from Ali ibn al-Fadl al-Karabisi, from Ibn Uyayna."
"7695","7695 - Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Uqayli and Azhar ibn Jamil narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The worst food is the food of the wedding feast; the rich is invited to it and the poor is left, and whoever does not answer it has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger. And others besides Ayyub narrate from al-Zuhri, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayra."
"7696","7696 - And Ahmad ibn Abda narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: Sufyan, meaning al-Thawri, narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra."
"7697","7697 - And Ubayd ibn Isma'il al-Habbari narrated it to us, he said: Abu Usama narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he prayed over the Negus and said four takbirs over him. And we do not know that the trustworthy narrators supported from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, anything other than this hadith. And more than one narrated it from Ubaydullah."
"7698","7698 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Bahz narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The strong is not the one who throws in wrestling, but the strong is the one who controls himself in anger. And this hadith others besides Malik have narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayra, and Malik said: from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id."
"7699","7699 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra: that he said: If I saw gazelles grazing in Medina I would not drive them away, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is between its two lava tracts is sanctuary. And this hadith others besides Malik have narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, so we limited ourselves to Malik."
"7700","7700 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Malik, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When a man says to his companion on Friday, be quiet, he has engaged in idle talk. And this hadith Ibn Uyayna and others have narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra."
"7701","7701 - Humayd ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, he said: Ma'n ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), al-Adba, was not beaten, then a Bedouin came on a young camel and beat her, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is a right upon Allah that He does not raise anything of this world except that He brings it down. And this hadith, we do not know anyone raised it except Malik, nor from him except Ma'n. Ma'n said: Malik would not narrate it musnad, then one day he came out to us lively and narrated it to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra."
"7702","7702 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah has cursed a people who took the graves of their prophets as mosques. And this hadith others besides Malik have narrated, from al-Zuhri, among them al-Layth, and Ibn Jurayj and Fulayh ibn Sulayman and others."
"7703","7703 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us with it, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7704","7704 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated it to us with it, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7705","7705 - Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah has cursed the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as mosques."
"7706","7706 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra: that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, does one of us pray in a single garment? He said: Do all of you find two garments? And this hadith Ibn Uyayna has narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra. And others besides them narrated it, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id and Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra."
"7707","7707 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Malik and Ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. And this hadith Ma'mar has narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id and Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra."
"7708","7708 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, he said: Malik and Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats from this foul-smelling tree, or the vile, let him not come near our mosque."
"7709","7709 - And al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats from this tree, meaning garlic, let him not harm us in our mosque. And we do not know anyone narrated it from Malik except Rawh, so he joined Malik and Salih together, and I think he carried the hadith of Malik onto the hadith of Salih. And it is only known from the hadith of Malik, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, mursal."
"7710","7710 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he announced the Negus on the day he died, and went out with them to the prayer place, and prayed with them and said four takbirs over him. And this hadith a group have narrated, among them Ibn Uyayna and others, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, and Yunus ibn Ishaq narrated it, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id and Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra."
"7711","7711 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No three children of any Muslim die and Fire touches him except as fulfillment of the oath. And this hadith Ibn Uyayna also narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra."
"7712","7712 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Maslama narrated to us, from Malik, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The congregational prayer is better than the prayer of one of you alone by twenty-five prayers. And this hadith was narrated from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id and Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra."
"7713","7713 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you finish the ending of Umm al-Kitab, say Amin, so whoever's saying Amin coincides with the Amin of the angels, his past sins are forgiven, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say Amin. And this hadith Ibn Uyayna has narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra. And Yunus narrated it, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id and Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra."
"7714","7714 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, from his brother, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I was commanded to fight the people until they say there is no god but Allah, so whoever says there is no god but Allah has protected his wealth and blood from me, and his reckoning is upon Allah."
"7715","7715 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la informed us, he said: Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When Khosrow perishes there will be no Khosrow after him, and when Caesar perishes there will be no Caesar after him, and by the One in whose hand is my soul, their treasures will be spent in the path of Allah. And this hadith Ibn Uyayna has narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7716","7716 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la informed us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The example of the believer is like the crop, the wind keeps bending it, and the believer keeps being struck by trial, and the example of the hypocrite is like the pine tree, it keeps shaking until it is uprooted. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it except Ma'mar and Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id."
"7717","7717 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la informed us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and whoever waits for it until its burial is finished has two qirats. They said: What are they? He said: The two qirats are like two great mountains. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, except Ma'mar, and Ma'mar was contradicted in its isnad."
"7718","7718 - Hilal ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7719","7719 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la informed us, he said: Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whomever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in religion, and I am only a distributor and Allah gives. And Abd al-A'la said: I am only a distributor and Allah gives. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, except Ma'mar."
"7720","7720 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la informed us, he said: Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Time draws near, knowledge is taken away, miserliness is cast, trials appear, and harj increases. They said: What is harj? He said: Killing, killing. And this hadith we remember only from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, and Ma'mar was contradicted in it."
"7721","7721 - Ahmad ibn Abda narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was asked about a mouse that fell into ghee, he said: It is taken with what is around it and thrown away, I think he said: and the rest is eaten."
"7722","7722 - And Nasr ibn Ali narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-A'la informed us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: It is taken with what is around it and thrown away. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, except Ma'mar, and he was contradicted in its isnad and matn."
"7723","7723 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la informed us, he said: Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet, he said: Let none of you prevent his neighbor from placing a beam in his wall, then Abu Hurayra says: What is wrong with me that I see you turning away from it, I will surely throw it between your shoulders. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who said it from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, except Ma'mar, and others besides Ma'mar narrate it from al-Zuhri, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayra."
"7724","7724 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he narrates from his Lord, He, blessed and exalted, said: Every deed of the son of Adam is for him except fasting, it is Mine, and I reward for it, and the breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk."
"7725","7725 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la informed us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no newborn except that Satan pricks him except the son of Maryam and his mother. Abu Hurayra said: Recite if you wish: And I seek refuge for her with You and her offspring from the accursed Satan."
"7726","7726 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la informed us, and al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, both mentioned it from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: You will leave Medina in its finest state, none visits it except the seekers, meaning the seekers of predators and birds. And this hadith is remembered only from Ma'mar and Yunus."
"7727","7727 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pride and arrogance are among the loud-voiced owners of camels from the people of tents, and calmness is among the people of sheep, and faith is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni."
"7728","7728 - And al-Husayn narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: On the night I was taken, I was brought two vessels, in one of them wine and in the other milk, and it was said: Choose whichever you wish, so I chose milk, and it was said to me: You were guided to the fitra, or you hit the fitra, had you taken the wine your umma would have gone astray. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, more famous than Ma'mar, and he was contradicted in its isnad."
"7729","7729 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Every newborn is born upon the fitra, then his parents make him Jewish and Zoroastrian, just as the animal is produced whole, do you sense in it any cut-eared? I think he said: mutilated."
"7730","7730 - And al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a man said to him: Which deed is best? He said: Faith in Allah and jihad in the path of Allah. He said: Then what? He said: Then an accepted hajj. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it except al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra."
"7731","7731 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he proposed to Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, and she said: O Messenger of Allah, I have grown old and have children. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best women who rode camels are the righteous women of Quraysh, the most tender to a child in his childhood, and the most caring for a husband in his wealth. And this hadith Yunus also narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7732","7732 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la informed us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The dream of the believer is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"7733","7733 - And Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la informed us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Let no townsman sell for a Bedouin, and do not outbid one another, and let no man sell over his brother's sale, nor propose over his proposal, and let no woman ask for her sister's divorce to overturn her bowl. And this hadith others besides Ma'mar also narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra."
"7734","7734 - Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Abi Ayyub al-Raqqi informed us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la informed us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The congregational prayer exceeds a man's prayer alone by twenty-five, and the angels of the night and the angels of the day gather at the dawn prayer."
"7735","7735 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will appear in the end of time Dhu al-Suwayqatayn from Abyssinia, and he will destroy the Ka'ba. He said, or I think he said: He will demolish it."
"7736","7736 - Ahmad ibn Aban narrated it to us, he said: Sufyan, meaning Ibn Uyayna, narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There will appear in the end of time Dhu al-Suwayqatayn from Abyssinia, and he will destroy the Ka'ba."
"7737","7737 - And Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ibrahim ibn Abi Qutayla narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Sa'd, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"7738","7738 - And Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated it to us with it, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, from al-Layth, he said: Yunus narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar to the first."
"7739","7739 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from Urwa, from A'isha, they said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seclude the last ten of Ramadan until Allah took him."
"7740","7740 - And al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered while the Abyssinians were playing with their spears in the mosque, so Umar scolded them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave them, O Umar, for they are the sons of Arfida."
"7741","7741 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Sinan narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of the mujahid in the path of Allah, and Allah knows best who strives in His path, is like the fasting, standing, humble, bowing, prostrating one."
"7742","7742 - Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn al-Ru'as narrated to us, he said: Kudayr, a neighbor of Abu Asim, narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The pledge is not forfeited from its owner who pledged it, its gain is his and its loss is upon him. Thus this shaykh narrated it. And Malik narrated it, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, mursal, except Isma'il ibn Ayyash, who narrated it from Ibn Abi Dhi'b and Ibn Abi Unaysa, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7743","7743 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Ahwazi narrated it to us with it, he said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Isma'il narrated to us, and he wrote to Muhammad ibn Humayd informing me that Ibrahim ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to him, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7744","7744 (m) - Al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated it to us with it, he said: Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Unaysa narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith, those who sent it mursal are more reliable than those who joined it."
"7745","7745 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar and Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There is no fara' and no atira. He said: Abu Ishaq said: Ali and Ibn Mas'ud did not observe fara' nor atira."
"7746","7746 - And Muhammad ibn Ziyad and Ahmad ibn Abda narrated it to us with it, from Ibn Uyayna, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we do not know Shu'ba narrated musnad from Ma'mar except this hadith and a hadith differed about, which Abbad ibn Abbad narrated."
"7747","7747 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: al-Firyabi Muhammad ibn Yusuf informed us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: In Paradise is a tree under whose shade a rider travels a hundred years and does not cross it. Recite if you wish: And extended shade. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it musnad from Ibn Uyayna except al-Firyabi."
"7748","7748 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi informed us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet, that he said: The orphan girl is consulted about herself, and her silence is her consent. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it musnad from Ibn Uyayna except al-Firyabi."
"7749","7749 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq ibn Bukayr and Hammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Anbasa narrated to us, they said: Umar ibn Habib narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Allah has ninety-nine names, whoever enumerates them enters Paradise. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Ibn Uyayna except Umar ibn Habib, and he was a man from Basra from Banu Adi, and he was not a memorizer."
"7750","7750 - Sa'dan ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, and from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man complained to him that he finds something in prayer. He said: Let him not turn away until he finds a smell or hears a sound. And this hadith, the companions of Ibn Uyayna narrate it from Ibn Uyayna, from al-Zuhri, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle. And we do not know anyone who said: from Ibn Uyayna, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, except al-Haytham."
"7751","7751 - Zam'a followed al-Haytham, and narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with something like that. Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated it to us with it, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Zam'a narrated to us."
"7752","7752 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The righteous owned slave has two rewards, and by the One in whose hand is Abu Hurayra's soul, were it not for hajj and jihad I would not care except to die as a slave."
"7753","7753 - Al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Jarawi narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Suwayd al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woman was created from a rib; if you go to straighten it you break her, and if you leave her you enjoy her while there is crookedness in her."
"7754","7754 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Ya'mar ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, blessed and exalted, will grasp the earth on the Day of Resurrection and fold the heaven with His right hand, then say: I am the King, where are the kings of the earth?"
"7755","7755 - Ahmad ibn al-Faraj al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he returned from his expedition at Khaybar, traveled his night until when drowsiness overtook him he halted, and said to Bilal: Guard the night for us, so Bilal prayed what was decreed for him, and the Messenger of Allah and his companions slept, meaning: when dawn drew near Bilal leaned against his mount facing the qibla, and his eyes overcame him while leaning against his mount, and neither the Prophet nor Bilal nor any of his companions woke until the sun struck them, and the Messenger of Allah was the first of them to wake, so the Messenger of Allah was alarmed, and Bilal said: What took your soul took mine, may my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah, so the Messenger of Allah performed ablution and commanded Bilal, and he called the iqama, and he prayed the dawn with them, and when he finished it he said: Whoever forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it, for Allah, blessed and exalted, said: And establish prayer for My remembrance."
"7756","7756 - And this hadith, Abu Musa narrated it to us with it, he said: Sa'id ibn Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Salih, meaning Ibn Abi al-Akhdar, narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"7757","7757 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Ya'mar ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The best charity is what is from sufficiency, and begin with those you support."
"7758","7758 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Musafir, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"7759","7759 - Ahmad ibn al-Faraj al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The oath promotes the goods and erases blessing. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri except Yunus."
"7760","7760 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whichever believer I have abused, make that a means of nearness for him to You on the Day of Resurrection."
"7761","7761 - Al-Abbas ibn Ja'far narrated it to us with it, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ibn Akhi al-Zuhri, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"7762","7762 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib narrated to me, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you rises at night, let him not put his hand into the vessel until he pours over it twice or thrice, for none of you knows where his hand spent the night. And this hadith Ibn Uyayna narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra."
"7763","7763 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri narrated to me, he said: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib narrated to me, from Abu Hurayra: that he heard him saying: People recited with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a prayer in which he recited loudly, and when the Messenger of Allah finished his prayer he turned to them and said: Did any of you recite with me just now? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I say, why am I being contested in the Qur'an. And this hadith Ibn Uyayna and Ma'mar and a group of al-Zuhri's companions narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Ukayma, from Abu Hurayra, and that is correct, and some of al-Zuhri's companions said, from al-Zuhri, he said: I heard Ibn Ukayma narrating to Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, and al-Awza'i erred in its isnad and said: from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, and Ibn Akhi al-Zuhri narrated it, from al-Zuhri, from al-A'raj, from Ibn Buhayna, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and erred in its isnad."
"7764","7764 - Sadaqa ibn al-Fadl al-Ammi narrated to us, he said: Abu Damra Anas ibn Iyad al-Laythi narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra: that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: O Messenger of Allah, do You see what we do, is it something finished or something begun anew? He said: Rather something already finished. He said: Then for what is action? He said: Each is facilitated for what he was created for. And this hadith more than one have narrated from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, that Umar. And we do not know anyone narrated it musnad from al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, except Anas ibn Iyad. And Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated it, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that Umar."
"7765","7765 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Juwayriya al-Anazi narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the Muslim upon the Muslim are five: greeting when he meets him, visiting the sick, following funerals, answering the invitation, and blessing the sneezer."
"7766","7766 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, he said: Murajim ibn al-Awwam ibn Murajim narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, he said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, and horses rush with us, and a speaker said: O Messenger of Allah, was this in the prior decree? He said: Yes. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle with this isnad, and we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Awza'i except Murajim."
"7767","7767 - Ahmad ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): You will surely leave it, meaning Medina, in its best state, made easy for the seekers, meaning predators and birds."
"7768","7768 - And Ahmad ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Suwayd said, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is black seed, for in it is healing from every disease except death. And this hadith Ibn Uyayna narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7769","7769 - And Ahmad ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, he raised it, he said: Allah, blessed and exalted, says: Fasting is Mine and I reward for it, and the breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk."
"7770","7770 - Ahmad ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade continuous fasting in fasting, and they said: You fast continuously. He said: Who among you is like me; I spend the night, my Lord feeds me and gives me drink."
"7771","7771 - And Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever keeps a dog that is not a hunting dog nor livestock, a qirat is deducted from his reward every day."
"7772","7772 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah made mercy a hundred parts, and kept ninety-nine with Him, and sent down one part on earth, and from that is mercy among creatures, until an animal lifts its hoof from its young fearing to kill it."
"7773","7773 - Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Ibn al-Had, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw Amr ibn Amir al-Khuza'i dragging his intestines in the Fire, and he was the first who let loose the sa'iba camels. Abu Bakr said: And I think between Ibn al-Had and al-Zuhri is Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abi Bakr."
"7774","7774 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, he said: Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The Hour will not come until a fire emerges from the land of Hijaz illuminating, I think he said, from it the necks of camels at Busra. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, except Uqayl, and Uqayl was contradicted in his narration from al-Zuhri."
"7775","7775 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, he said: Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is not stung from one hole twice."
"7776","7776 - And al-Abbas ibn Ja'far al-Baghdadi narrated it to us with it, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: Ibn Akhi al-Zuhri narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet, with something similar. And Zam'a narrated it, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father. And al-Walid ibn Muhammad narrated it, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from A'isha, and the hadith is the hadith of Abu Hurayra."
"7777","7777 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Hour will not come until the buttocks of the women of Daws shake around Dhu al-Khalasa. And al-Khalasa is what they used to worship in ignorance."
"7778","7778 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that Abu Hurayra said: While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: While I was standing in Paradise, a woman was performing ablution beside a palace. I said: Whose palace is this? They said: Umar's. So I remembered his jealousy and turned away. Al-Zuhri said: So Umar wept. He said: Over you I am jealous, O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you."
"7779","7779 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, he said: Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib informed me, from Abu Hurayra, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I was sent with comprehensive speech, and aided with awe, and while I was sleeping I was brought the treasures of the earth and placed in my hand. And this hadith Ma'mar narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id and Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra."
"7780","7780 - Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib informed me, from Abu Hurayra: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled for one who committed zina without being married, with exile of a year along with establishing the hadd upon him. And this hadith others besides Uqayl narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Abu Hurayra and Zayd ibn Khalid, and Ibn Uyayna and Shibl said."
"7781","7781 - Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, that Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib informed him that Abu Hurayra informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While I was sleeping I saw myself at the head of a well with a bucket on it, and I drew what Allah willed, then Ibn Abi Quhafa took it and drew a bucket or two buckets, and in his drawing was weakness, and Allah forgives him, then it turned into a large bucket, and Umar took it, and I did not see a genius among people drawing Umar's drawing, until people struck camels at the watering place."
"7782","7782 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My example and the example of the messengers is like a palace fine in its building, people find no fault in it except the place of a brick, so I was the brick and the building was completed."
"7783","7783 - Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever sleeps with grease on his hand and something befalls him, let him blame only himself. And this hadith Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq and Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Ibn Abbas. And Ibn Uyayna narrated it, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, mursal. And Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated it, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from A'isha."
"7784","7784 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Wa'il, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7785","7785 - And Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghassan narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Wa'il, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the wording is the wording of Muhammad ibn al-Salt. He said: When you carry, delay the carrying, or from the carrying, for the leg is bound and the hand is suspended. And we do not know Bakr ibn Wa'il narrated from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, except this hadith."
"7786","7786 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Mihran ibn Abi Umar narrated to us, he said: Zam'a narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet, he said: The orphan girl is consulted about herself, and if she is silent it is her permission, or permission from her."
"7787","7787 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Nu'man, meaning Ibn Rashid, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you eats, let him eat with his right hand, for Satan eats with his left and drinks with his left. And this hadith a group narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Ubaydullah, from his grandfather Ibn Umar. And Ma'mar narrated it and said, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, and erred in it, and Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar followed him in it."
"7788","7788 - Muhammad ibn Musa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from al-Nu'man ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the worst of usury is a man's extending in his brother's honor. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri except al-Nu'man ibn Rashid, nor from al-Nu'man except Wuhayb, nor from Wuhayb except Muhammad ibn Abi Nu'aym, and al-Nu'man was narrated from by a group of eminent ones; among them: Ibn Jurayj, and Jarir ibn Hazim, and Wuhayb ibn Khalid."
"7789","7789 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sufyan narrated to us, from Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade malaqih and madamin and habal al-habala. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, except Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar, and he was not a memorizer."
"7790","7790 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Khaybar, he promised the Jews to give them half the fruit on condition they cultivate it, then: I keep you as long as Allah keeps you, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to send Abdullah ibn Rawaha to estimate it, then give them choice to take it or leave it, and the Jews came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in some of that and complained to him about his estimation, so he called Abdullah ibn Rawaha and mentioned to him what they mentioned, and Abdullah said: It is what I have, O Messenger of Allah, if they wish they take it, and if they leave it we take it, so the Jews were satisfied and said: By this the heavens and earth stand, then the Messenger of Allah said in his illness in which he died: Two religions shall not gather in the Arabian Peninsula, and when that was conveyed to Umar he sent to the Jews of Khaybar and said: The Messenger of Allah gave you ownership of these properties, and stipulated for you that we keep you as long as Allah keeps you, and Allah has permitted your expulsion, so Umar expelled every Jew and Christian from the land of Hijaz, then divided it among the people of Medina. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, except Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar."
"7791","7791 - Amr ibn Ali and Abu Kamil narrated to us, and the wording is Amr's, they said: Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you hear the mu'adhdhin, say as he says. And this hadith a group besides Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated and said: from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Sa'id, and that is correct."
"7792","7792 - And Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, he said: Aban ibn Sa'id al-Akbar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after Allah had given him Khaybar, and asked him to allot for him and his companions, and he did not do so. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it except Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz."
"7793","7793 - Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Salim, from al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that he heard Abu Hurayra describing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: He was a man of medium stature, closer to tall, intensely white, black-bearded, with fine hair, with long eyelashes, wide between the shoulders, stepping with his whole foot together, having no hollow of the foot, turning all together and turning away all together, I never saw his like before nor after. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, except al-Zubaydi, and he is a famous man."
"7794","7794 - Salama ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughira Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Mubashshir ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Zuhri narrating from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Protection is two protections: protection of chastity, and protection of marriage. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayra except from this angle, nor do we know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle with this isnad. And Mubashshir ibn Ubayd is weak in hadith, and Baqiyya ibn al-Walid and Yazid ibn Harun and others narrated from him."
"7795","7795 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi' narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamza narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id and Ata ibn Zayd, that Abu Hurayra informed them that people said: O Messenger of Allah, will we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you dispute about the moon on the night of full moon with no cloud below it? They said: No. He said: Do you dispute about the sun with no cloud below it? They said: No. He said: You will see Him likewise. People will be detained on the Day of Resurrection, then it will be said: Whoever used to worship something, let him follow it. Among them is one who follows the sun, among them one who follows the moon, among them one who follows the tyrants, and this umma remains, with its hypocrites in it, and He, blessed and exalted, comes to them and says: I am your Lord. They say: You are our Lord. Then the bridge is struck across the midst of Hell, and I will be the first of the messengers to cross with my umma, and none speaks that day except the messengers, and the supplication of the messengers that day is: O Allah, save, save. And in Hell are hooks like the thorn of al-Sa'dan. Have you seen the thorn of al-Sa'dan? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: They are like the thorn of al-Sa'dan, snatching people by their deeds. Among them is one mangled, or he said: torn, and among them one who is saved, until when Allah, blessed and exalted, intends mercy for whom He wills of the people of the Fire, Allah, blessed and exalted, commands the angels to bring out whoever used to worship Allah, and they bring them out recognizing them by the marks of prostration. Allah has forbidden the Fire to eat the mark of prostration. So they emerge from the Fire charred, and water of life is poured over them, and they grow as a grain grows in the flood's carried soil. Then Allah, blessed and exalted, finishes judging between servants. And while a man is between Paradise and Fire, he is the last of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise, facing the Fire with his face, and says: O Lord, turn my face from the Fire, for its wind has poisoned me and its flame has burned me. He, blessed and exalted, says: Perhaps if I do that for you, you will ask Me for other than that. He says: No, by Your might. And he gives his Lord what He wills of covenant and pledge. So Allah turns his face from the Fire. When he turns to Paradise and sees its splendor, he is silent as long as Allah wills him to be silent, then says: O Lord, bring me to the gate of Paradise. Allah, blessed and exalted, says: Did you not give covenants and pledges that you would not ask for other than what you asked? He says: O Lord, let me not be the most wretched of Your creation. He says: Perhaps if I give you, you will ask Me for other? He says: No, by Your might, I will not ask You for other than that. And he gives his Lord what He wills of covenant and pledge. So Allah, blessed and exalted, brings him to the gate of Paradise. When he reaches its gate it opens for him, and he sees its blossom and what is in it of freshness and joy, and is silent as long as Allah wills him to be silent, then says: O Lord, admit me to Paradise. He, blessed and exalted, says: O son of Adam, how treacherous you are. You gave covenants and pledges that you would not ask for other than what you were given. He says: O Lord, do not make me the most wretched of Your creation. He, blessed and exalted, laughs at him, then permits him to enter Paradise, then says: Wish. And he wishes, until when his wishes are cut off, Allah, blessed and exalted, says: Such, his Lord reminding him, until when his wishes end, Allah, exalted, says: For you is that and its like with it. Abu Sa'id al-Khudri said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That and ten times its like. Abu Hurayra said: I remembered from the Messenger of Allah only that he said: For you is that and its like with it. Abu Sa'id said: I bear witness I heard him saying: For you is that and ten times its like. And this hadith Ma'mar and Ibrahim ibn Sa'd and others narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Hurayra and Abu Sa'id, and we do not know anyone joined Ata ibn Yazid and Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib except Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamza, and Mu'awiya ibn Yahya al-Sadafi agreed on Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib and Ata ibn Yazid, and Shu'ayb is more reliable."
"7796","7796 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq ibn Umar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Three do not smell the scent of Paradise: a man who claims to other than his father, a man who lies about his prophet, and a man who lies about his eyes. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, except Abd al-Razzaq ibn Umar, and he is a man from Damascus. And some who narrated from him said: al-Ayli, and we do not know this wording narrated from Abu Hurayra except with this isnad. And Yahya ibn Hassan and Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud and al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated from Abd al-Razzaq ibn Umar."
"7797","7797 - Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn Sayf al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, from his father, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you yawns in prayer, let him place his hand over his mouth. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, except Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud, nor do we know anyone narrated it from Sulayman except his son Muhammad, and Muhammad ibn Sulayman narrated from his father narrations not followed in, and the people of knowledge accepted his hadith and narrated from him."
"7798","7798 - Ali ibn Muslim and Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mulhami al-Duba'i narrated to us, and the wording is Muhammad ibn al-Abbas's, they said: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever enters a horse between two horses while he is safe from being beaten is gambling, and whoever enters a horse between two horses while he does not care whether he is beaten is not gambling. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, except Sufyan ibn Husayn. Ahmad said: Thus I found it in my book."
"7799","7799 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Mufaddal ibn Ziyad narrated to me, from al-Sadafi, meaning Mu'awiya ibn Yahya, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Seventy thousand of my umma will enter Paradise, their faces shining like the moon on the night of full moon. Abu Hurayra said: So Ukkasha ibn Mihsan al-Asadi stood, and raised a striped cloak on him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me among them. He said: O Allah, make him among them. Abu Hurayra said: Then another stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me among them. He said: Ukkasha has preceded you with it. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except Mu'awiya, nor do we know anyone narrated it from Mu'awiya except al-Mufaddal, and we already mentioned Mu'awiya with weakness, so we sufficed from repeating his mention after. Though we do not know anyone narrated from him more upright in hadith from him than al-Mufaddal ibn Ziyad, so I see he narrated to him from a book."
"7800","7800 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Anbasa al-Haddad, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Speech about destiny was delayed for the worst of this umma in the end of time, and disputation about the Qur'an is disbelief. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, except Anbasa. And he is weak in hadith, he was alone with this hadith from al-Zuhri's hadith."
